s","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dever-labs/ngx-mfe-broker/commits/074da655fe86146e4396529f20e440e6842eab73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:22:32Z","email":"casper.elkrog@dever.dk","name":"czprz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T21:22:32Z","email":"casper.elkrog@dever.dk","name":"czprz"},"message":"refactor: remove searchOpen and openSearch from MfeStateService\n\nCross-tab event triggers (like opening a command palette) are app-specific\nconcerns. Consumers can model them as a numeric key in their own state\ncontract, relying on the generic get/set/cross-tab sync that MfeStateService\nalready provides.\n\n- Remove searchOpen signal, openSearch(), searchChannel, SEARCH_CHANNEL_NAME\n- ngOnDestroy now closes only the single state channel\n- Update spec: drop 2 search channel tests, add numeric counter test (28 total)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"531ea170d5bb18966ae57bbdcbed732bed51e163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dever-labs/ngx-mfe-broker/git/trees/531ea170d5bb18966ae57bbdcbed732bed51e163"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dever-labs/ngx-mfe-broker/git/commits/074da655fe86146e4396529f20e440e6842eab73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57328905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/czprz/gists{/gist_id