","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zrmnelson","id":104142635,"login":"zrmnelson","node_id":"U_kgDOBjUXKw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/b9713992480a1ee9eeae6964c52da6ce41c6adb8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:47:24Z","email":"104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zeno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T08:47:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MYAH-353: isolate Inbox reply drafts per Campaign context (#162)\n\n* MYAH-353: isolate Inbox reply drafts per Campaign context\n\nBackend:\n- add the paged Email reply-context options query with exact target/Creator\n  authorization, permission-scoped outbound evidence, stable keyset cursors and\n  fail-closed General provenance (never inferred from a null association)\n- add core.myahInboxReplyContextDraft storage keyed by workspace, immutable\n  contact anchor, channel, exact target and context, with CAS, revision-zero\n  semantics, context fingerprints and partial uniqueness\n- add Email v2 approval/send authority with immutable snapshots, target-first\n  sibling reservation, target-wide pending/unknown authority and provider I/O\n  kept outside database locks\n- split Email release A (compatibility schema, guards, provenance) from release\n  B (preservation and activation), and freeze dedicated legacy Email writers\n\nFrontend:\n- carry the full anchored draft identity through autosave, reads, readiness and\n  send instead of a workspace/thread-only key\n- resolve execution state from an exact post-save reread, treat a fresh\n  authorized NEEDS_REVIEW read as authoritative, and gate explicit conflict\n  adoption behind a current-capability metadata reread\n- keep one main composer: the thread selector pins the exact delivery target and\n  the Campaign travels with the selected thread\n- keep the composer surface and its controls when no draft can be loaded, and\n  never render status copy into the reply surface\n\nFixes found by running the isolated PostgreSQL suites and the full server\nsuite: a text/uuid comparison in the Inbox reply target execution-state query,\nand a missing column type on the reply-context draft entity.\n\n* MYAH-353: re-slot upgrade commands above the existing 2-20 sequence\n\nThe four new upgrade commands used timestamps 1789313971535-1789313971538.\nThe first collided exactly with the existing\nSynchronizeCampaignLifecycleStatusMetadataCommand (1789313971535), which the\nappend-only CI guard rejects: a new upgrade command must sort strictly after\nevery existing command in the same version directory, because the upgrade\ncursor tracks a single last-applied position.\n\nRe-slotted all four to the real authoring epoch, preserving the Release A /\nRelease B ordering:\n\n  1789645911001  create reply-context drafts      (Release A, fast instance)\n  1789645911002  migrate reply-context drafts     (Release B, workspace)\n  1789645911003  create Email General provenance  (Release A, fast instance)\n  1789645911004  install provenance trigger       (Release A, workspace)\n\nFiles renamed, decorator timestamps updated, and every importer plus the\ndurable-name assertion in the module spec updated.\n\n* MYAH-353: record the composer''s message references in the Lingui catalogs\n\nThe merged composer renders the existing \"Send\" and \"Send reply\" messages\nfrom MyahInboxReplyWorkspace, so lingui:extract adds that file as an\nadditional reference for both ids. Regenerated and committed the catalogs so\nthe front CI gate (extract -> compile -> clean locales tree) passes.\n\nHoisted the composer''s single `t`Send reply`` call site to one constant so\nthe catalog records one reference instead of a duplicate.\n\n* MYAH-353: skip schema-less workspaces and seed drafts contextually\n\nCI''s cross-version upgrade aborted with \"Upgrade completed with 2 workspace\nfailure(s)\": the provenance trigger install ran for workspaces that have no\nprovisioned database schema, so CREATE TRIGGER failed with\n`schema \"workspace_...\" does not exist`.\n\nBoth Email workspace commands now skip a workspace whose derived schema does\nnot exist, matching the existing SynchronizeMyahStandardMetadataCommand\npattern, and the install command gained a regression covering the skip path.\n\nThe shared Task 7 integration fixture and the Task 7 spec still seeded and read\nEmail drafts through the retired thread-only columns. The contextual save\nrequires expectedWorkspaceId and the legacy writer is frozen, so both now read\nand write through the contextual draft API instead.\n\n* MYAH-353: keep the interaction-context CHECK permissive for unmatched rows\n\nThe Email v2 work re-added CHK_ACTION_APPROVAL_BINDING_INTERACTION_CONTEXT as\n`CHECK ((...) IS TRUE)`. PostgreSQL passes a CHECK when its expression is NULL,\nbut `NULL IS TRUE` is FALSE, so the wrapper rejected any row matching no branch\n— including Instagram bindings that leave actionKind unset, which main''s bare\n`CHECK (...)` tolerated.\n\nThe instance command and the entity now both use the bare CHECK again, with a\ncomment recording why. Rows that do match an Email branch but carry an invalid\nsnapshot still evaluate to FALSE and are still rejected.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): restore strict interaction-context CHECK constraint\n\nThe prior commit stripped IS TRUE off CHK_ACTION_APPROVAL_BINDING_INTERACTION_CONTEXT,\nwhich lets a row matching no branch pass the CHECK (Postgres treats a NULL\nCHECK result as satisfied). Its justification claimed main used a bare\nCHECK; main already had IS TRUE. Restored the strict wrapper in the entity,\nthe matching fast instance-command migration SQL, and the test that had\nbeen flipped to assert the weakened behavior.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): activate Email reply context on first use\n\nWorkspaces created directly at the current schema version never replay the\n2.20.0 upgrade command that activates Email reply context, so every new\nworkspace was permanently blocked with ''Email reply context activation is\npending''. assertEmailContextActivationEnabled now self-activates via the\nexisting idempotent preflightEmailWorkspace cutover instead of only relying\non the historical upgrade command.\n\n* feat(myah-inbox): support Email drafts on threads with no linked Creator\n\nSomeone can reply manually to an inbox email that hasn''t been linked to a\nCreator yet; that shouldn''t be blocked. Added an EMAIL_THREAD contact-anchor\nbranch to the reply-context evidence resolver (General context only, since\nCampaign eligibility can''t be evaluated without a Creator). Split the\nexisting test that had bundled ''reject thread anchors'' together with the\nCreator-isolation security check: kept the isolation check intact, replaced\nthe rejection assertion with a positive-path check that a creator-less\nthread draft persists independently of who the thread later gets relinked\nto.\n\n* test(myah-inbox): migrate mutation integration spec to context-scoped drafts\n\nSaveMyahInboxDraftInput dropped the flat threadId field for target/replyContext/\nexpectedWorkspaceId, and drafts moved from messageThread columns to\ncore.myahInboxReplyContextDraft, but this file was never updated. Rewrote the\ntwo draft tests onto an EMAIL_THREAD/General anchor (this thread is never\nlinked to a Creator), revision numbering starting at 0 to match the new\nstorage, and assertions against the new draft table.\n\n* style(myah-inbox): fix oxfmt formatting\n\n* test(myah-inbox): seed real outbound evidence for the Task 7 draft thread\n\nEvery message on this shared fixture''s draft thread was seeded as INCOMING,\nso the Creator+Campaign combination never had delivered-correspondence\nevidence. Saving a Campaign-context draft on it now correctly requires that\nevidence (a pre-existing rule, unrelated to this branch); the fixture just\nnever satisfied it. This was invisible while the Email-context activation\ngate failed first on every attempt; fixing that surfaced this next.\n\nAdds one new outgoing message fixture (additive only, no existing fixture\nentries changed) so the eligibility check has real evidence to find.\n\n* chore: retrigger CI (GitHub did not start workflows for the previous push)\n\n* test(myah-inbox): fix stale constructor call sites after MYAH-354 merge\n\nMyahInboxMutationService and MessagingSaveMessagesAndEnqueueContactCreationService\nboth gained new required constructor parameters (contact-triage dependencies)\non main. These three test files construct them positionally and were left\nwith stale argument lists after the merge; this was caught by the full unit\ntest sweep, not the merge itself.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): fix two CI failures surfaced only after unblocking activation/eligibility\n\n1. instagram-action-budget.integration-spec.ts: this pre-existing test''s raw\n   INSERT into actionApprovalBinding never set actionKind, silently relying\n   on the bare/permissive CHECK constraint the last commit temporarily\n   introduced. Restoring the strict IS TRUE wrapper (already done earlier\n   this session) correctly rejects it. Fixed the test to set actionKind =\n   ''REPLY'', matching the actual reservations it seeds.\n\n2. myah-inbox-reply-proposal.integration-spec.ts: GenerateMyahInboxReplyProposalInput\n   extends MyahInboxReplyDraftInput (this PR''s new base input), but this\n   test was never updated off the old flat {threadId, operatorInstructions}\n   shape. Migrated to target/replyContext/expectedWorkspaceId, matching the\n   Campaign-context identity the shared Task 7 fixture already sets up for\n   this thread.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): fix two more myah-assistant-skills failures caused by my own fixture edit\n\nBoth traced back to the evidence message I added to the shared Task 7\nfixture earlier this session:\n\n1. It became the newest message on the draft thread (09:30 > all others),\n   so a test picking ''the latest message on this thread'' picked it instead\n   of the message it was actually written for. Moved its timestamp to the\n   earliest slot instead \\u2014 it only needs to exist and be outbound, not be\n   recent.\n\n2. The fixture''s reported draftRevision now reflects the new per-Campaign\n   draft API, but the AI tool''s save_myah_inbox_reply_draft still reads/\n   writes the legacy per-thread columns directly, which the fixture no\n   longer touches. The two numbers diverged. Query the actual legacy\n   column value instead of relying on the fixture''s draftRevision.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): supply expectedContextFingerprint for generateMyahInboxReplyProposal\n\nGenerateMyahInboxReplyProposalInput requires expectedContextFingerprint,\nwhich the test never supplied. Reads it from myahInboxReplyDraft first,\nmatching the read-before-write pattern the fixture util already uses\nelsewhere.\n\n* MYAH-353: restore the Myah assistant Inbox draft-save tool path\n\nsaveMyahInboxDraft() now requires the operator-chosen Campaign context\n(target/replyContext) and rejects the old threadId-only shape. The\nMyah assistant chat tool''s save_myah_inbox_reply_draft handler still\ncalled it with the old shape, so every AI-tool-driven draft save\nsilently failed with a stale CONFLICT and nothing was ever persisted.\n\nAdd MyahInboxMutationService#saveMyahInboxDraftForThread, which\nderives the same Creator/thread anchor the Inbox read APIs already\nexpose from just a threadId and saves a General (no-Campaign) draft\nthrough the same per-context draft store the composer uses. Wire the\ntool handler to it, and update the tests that had pinned the broken\nrejection as expected behavior.\n\nAlso fixes myah-inbox-reply-proposal.integration-spec.ts, which\nqueried contextFingerprint directly on MyahInboxReplyContextDraft\ninstead of its nested resolvedContext field.\n\n* MYAH-353: fix merge fallout in the 2.20.0 upgrade sequence spec\n\nAfter merging main''s CatchUpCampaignActivityControlMetadataWorkspaceCommand\nalongside this branch''s own new 2.20.0 commands, the pending-workspace-\ncommands assertion needed both newly registered commands, not just\nmain''s.\n\n* MYAH-353: reconcile current main after rebase\n\n* MYAH-353: reconcile MYAH-359 rebase fallout\n\n* MYAH-353: refresh generated GraphQL ordering\n\n* MYAH-353: update composer boundary assertion after rebase","tree":{"sha":"f0d41a8451c1ea5c13aab8f9651587e485ce1cdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/git/trees/f0d41a8451c1ea5c13aab8f9651587e485ce1cdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/git/commits/b9713992480a1ee9eeae6964c52da6ce41c6adb8","verification":{"payload":"tree f0d41a8451c1ea5c13aab8f9651587e485ce1cdd\nparent 321fd5572968c40a7a7011ed028602db56e13887\nauthor zeno <104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com> 1789894044 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789894044 +0530\n\nMYAH-353: isolate Inbox reply drafts per Campaign context (#162)\n\n* MYAH-353: isolate Inbox reply drafts per Campaign context\n\nBackend:\n- add the paged Email reply-context options query with exact target/Creator\n  authorization, permission-scoped outbound evidence, stable keyset cursors and\n  fail-closed General provenance (never inferred from a null association)\n- add core.myahInboxReplyContextDraft storage keyed by workspace, immutable\n  contact anchor, channel, exact target and context, with CAS, revision-zero\n  semantics, context fingerprints and partial uniqueness\n- add Email v2 approval/send authority with immutable snapshots, target-first\n  sibling reservation, target-wide pending/unknown authority and provider I/O\n  kept outside database locks\n- split Email release A (compatibility schema, guards, provenance) from release\n  B (preservation and activation), and freeze dedicated legacy Email writers\n\nFrontend:\n- carry the full anchored draft identity through autosave, reads, readiness and\n  send instead of a workspace/thread-only key\n- resolve execution state from an exact post-save reread, treat a fresh\n  authorized NEEDS_REVIEW read as authoritative, and gate explicit conflict\n  adoption behind a current-capability metadata reread\n- keep one main composer: the thread selector pins the exact delivery target and\n  the Campaign travels with the selected thread\n- keep the composer surface and its controls when no draft can be loaded, and\n  never render status copy into the reply surface\n\nFixes found by running the isolated PostgreSQL suites and the full server\nsuite: a text/uuid comparison in the Inbox reply target execution-state query,\nand a missing column type on the reply-context draft entity.\n\n* MYAH-353: re-slot upgrade commands above the existing 2-20 sequence\n\nThe four new upgrade commands used timestamps 1789313971535-1789313971538.\nThe first collided exactly with the existing\nSynchronizeCampaignLifecycleStatusMetadataCommand (1789313971535), which the\nappend-only CI guard rejects: a new upgrade command must sort strictly after\nevery existing command in the same version directory, because the upgrade\ncursor tracks a single last-applied position.\n\nRe-slotted all four to the real authoring epoch, preserving the Release A /\nRelease B ordering:\n\n  1789645911001  create reply-context drafts      (Release A, fast instance)\n  1789645911002  migrate reply-context drafts     (Release B, workspace)\n  1789645911003  create Email General provenance  (Release A, fast instance)\n  1789645911004  install provenance trigger       (Release A, workspace)\n\nFiles renamed, decorator timestamps updated, and every importer plus the\ndurable-name assertion in the module spec updated.\n\n* MYAH-353: record the composer''s message references in the Lingui catalogs\n\nThe merged composer renders the existing \"Send\" and \"Send reply\" messages\nfrom MyahInboxReplyWorkspace, so lingui:extract adds that file as an\nadditional reference for both ids. Regenerated and committed the catalogs so\nthe front CI gate (extract -> compile -> clean locales tree) passes.\n\nHoisted the composer''s single `t`Send reply`` call site to one constant so\nthe catalog records one reference instead of a duplicate.\n\n* MYAH-353: skip schema-less workspaces and seed drafts contextually\n\nCI''s cross-version upgrade aborted with \"Upgrade completed with 2 workspace\nfailure(s)\": the provenance trigger install ran for workspaces that have no\nprovisioned database schema, so CREATE TRIGGER failed with\n`schema \"workspace_...\" does not exist`.\n\nBoth Email workspace commands now skip a workspace whose derived schema does\nnot exist, matching the existing SynchronizeMyahStandardMetadataCommand\npattern, and the install command gained a regression covering the skip path.\n\nThe shared Task 7 integration fixture and the Task 7 spec still seeded and read\nEmail drafts through the retired thread-only columns. The contextual save\nrequires expectedWorkspaceId and the legacy writer is frozen, so both now read\nand write through the contextual draft API instead.\n\n* MYAH-353: keep the interaction-context CHECK permissive for unmatched rows\n\nThe Email v2 work re-added CHK_ACTION_APPROVAL_BINDING_INTERACTION_CONTEXT as\n`CHECK ((...) IS TRUE)`. PostgreSQL passes a CHECK when its expression is NULL,\nbut `NULL IS TRUE` is FALSE, so the wrapper rejected any row matching no branch\n— including Instagram bindings that leave actionKind unset, which main''s bare\n`CHECK (...)` tolerated.\n\nThe instance command and the entity now both use the bare CHECK again, with a\ncomment recording why. Rows that do match an Email branch but carry an invalid\nsnapshot still evaluate to FALSE and are still rejected.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): restore strict interaction-context CHECK constraint\n\nThe prior commit stripped IS TRUE off CHK_ACTION_APPROVAL_BINDING_INTERACTION_CONTEXT,\nwhich lets a row matching no branch pass the CHECK (Postgres treats a NULL\nCHECK result as satisfied). Its justification claimed main used a bare\nCHECK; main already had IS TRUE. Restored the strict wrapper in the entity,\nthe matching fast instance-command migration SQL, and the test that had\nbeen flipped to assert the weakened behavior.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): activate Email reply context on first use\n\nWorkspaces created directly at the current schema version never replay the\n2.20.0 upgrade command that activates Email reply context, so every new\nworkspace was permanently blocked with ''Email reply context activation is\npending''. assertEmailContextActivationEnabled now self-activates via the\nexisting idempotent preflightEmailWorkspace cutover instead of only relying\non the historical upgrade command.\n\n* feat(myah-inbox): support Email drafts on threads with no linked Creator\n\nSomeone can reply manually to an inbox email that hasn''t been linked to a\nCreator yet; that shouldn''t be blocked. Added an EMAIL_THREAD contact-anchor\nbranch to the reply-context evidence resolver (General context only, since\nCampaign eligibility can''t be evaluated without a Creator). Split the\nexisting test that had bundled ''reject thread anchors'' together with the\nCreator-isolation security check: kept the isolation check intact, replaced\nthe rejection assertion with a positive-path check that a creator-less\nthread draft persists independently of who the thread later gets relinked\nto.\n\n* test(myah-inbox): migrate mutation integration spec to context-scoped drafts\n\nSaveMyahInboxDraftInput dropped the flat threadId field for target/replyContext/\nexpectedWorkspaceId, and drafts moved from messageThread columns to\ncore.myahInboxReplyContextDraft, but this file was never updated. Rewrote the\ntwo draft tests onto an EMAIL_THREAD/General anchor (this thread is never\nlinked to a Creator), revision numbering starting at 0 to match the new\nstorage, and assertions against the new draft table.\n\n* style(myah-inbox): fix oxfmt formatting\n\n* test(myah-inbox): seed real outbound evidence for the Task 7 draft thread\n\nEvery message on this shared fixture''s draft thread was seeded as INCOMING,\nso the Creator+Campaign combination never had delivered-correspondence\nevidence. Saving a Campaign-context draft on it now correctly requires that\nevidence (a pre-existing rule, unrelated to this branch); the fixture just\nnever satisfied it. This was invisible while the Email-context activation\ngate failed first on every attempt; fixing that surfaced this next.\n\nAdds one new outgoing message fixture (additive only, no existing fixture\nentries changed) so the eligibility check has real evidence to find.\n\n* chore: retrigger CI (GitHub did not start workflows for the previous push)\n\n* test(myah-inbox): fix stale constructor call sites after MYAH-354 merge\n\nMyahInboxMutationService and MessagingSaveMessagesAndEnqueueContactCreationService\nboth gained new required constructor parameters (contact-triage dependencies)\non main. These three test files construct them positionally and were left\nwith stale argument lists after the merge; this was caught by the full unit\ntest sweep, not the merge itself.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): fix two CI failures surfaced only after unblocking activation/eligibility\n\n1. instagram-action-budget.integration-spec.ts: this pre-existing test''s raw\n   INSERT into actionApprovalBinding never set actionKind, silently relying\n   on the bare/permissive CHECK constraint the last commit temporarily\n   introduced. Restoring the strict IS TRUE wrapper (already done earlier\n   this session) correctly rejects it. Fixed the test to set actionKind =\n   ''REPLY'', matching the actual reservations it seeds.\n\n2. myah-inbox-reply-proposal.integration-spec.ts: GenerateMyahInboxReplyProposalInput\n   extends MyahInboxReplyDraftInput (this PR''s new base input), but this\n   test was never updated off the old flat {threadId, operatorInstructions}\n   shape. Migrated to target/replyContext/expectedWorkspaceId, matching the\n   Campaign-context identity the shared Task 7 fixture already sets up for\n   this thread.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): fix two more myah-assistant-skills failures caused by my own fixture edit\n\nBoth traced back to the evidence message I added to the shared Task 7\nfixture earlier this session:\n\n1. It became the newest message on the draft thread (09:30 > all others),\n   so a test picking ''the latest message on this thread'' picked it instead\n   of the message it was actually written for. Moved its timestamp to the\n   earliest slot instead \\u2014 it only needs to exist and be outbound, not be\n   recent.\n\n2. The fixture''s reported draftRevision now reflects the new per-Campaign\n   draft API, but the AI tool''s save_myah_inbox_reply_draft still reads/\n   writes the legacy per-thread columns directly, which the fixture no\n   longer touches. The two numbers diverged. Query the actual legacy\n   column value instead of relying on the fixture''s draftRevision.\n\n* fix(myah-inbox): supply expectedContextFingerprint for generateMyahInboxReplyProposal\n\nGenerateMyahInboxReplyProposalInput requires expectedContextFingerprint,\nwhich the test never supplied. Reads it from myahInboxReplyDraft first,\nmatching the read-before-write pattern the fixture util already uses\nelsewhere.\n\n* MYAH-353: restore the Myah assistant Inbox draft-save tool path\n\nsaveMyahInboxDraft() now requires the operator-chosen Campaign context\n(target/replyContext) and rejects the old threadId-only shape. The\nMyah assistant chat tool''s save_myah_inbox_reply_draft handler still\ncalled it with the old shape, so every AI-tool-driven draft save\nsilently failed with a stale CONFLICT and nothing was ever persisted.\n\nAdd MyahInboxMutationService#saveMyahInboxDraftForThread, which\nderives the same Creator/thread anchor the Inbox read APIs already\nexpose from just a threadId and saves a General (no-Campaign) draft\nthrough the same per-context draft store the composer uses. Wire the\ntool handler to it, and update the tests that had pinned the broken\nrejection as expected behavior.\n\nAlso fixes myah-inbox-reply-proposal.integration-spec.ts, which\nqueried contextFingerprint directly on MyahInboxReplyContextDraft\ninstead of its nested resolvedContext field.\n\n* MYAH-353: fix merge fallout in the 2.20.0 upgrade sequence spec\n\nAfter merging main''s CatchUpCampaignActivityControlMetadataWorkspaceCommand\nalongside this branch''s own new 2.20.0 commands, the pending-workspace-\ncommands assertion needed both newly registered commands, not just\nmain''s.\n\n* MYAH-353: reconcile current main after rebase\n\n* MYAH-353: reconcile MYAH-359 rebase fallout\n\n* MYAH-353: refresh generated GraphQL ordering\n\n* MYAH-353: update composer boundary assertion after rebase","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr52cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIVwQAKkctzPztaTTKwCxJ20ozagl\nbuxnxz4AjZOIOnvb0DFZ3A3J0CQsj0JYVi3JsW5ZufrgWTIl6secUh89qz6lqQ8w\nHLsHXulv2InnkBY01OpUYQLHB0qGhDdLpXqq3OtFVyXAcEA9hGkKog+Q311ZKfR8\noKwUivdUCi96wKr6BdtYNOTrk6KjEgHjvhx91PnH+GDv8h5l0lwxuq/Xue8JSCRc\nXKOxmgPdKfVxA1NeCteFX8hSl3DKpmfEP+ez8RU75voUCw0Bj3I6bxewoNTgP20e\n896Z6A4DVWn8v0q63rHpN9FCIHU8K5qNQbGsTNA9rb8nWVULGAsEo02axdZ5njr2\nliNjNJrPsoyCHU2eqzpw4M8Sdoi++OAbDPxHZ1aMgTfDsHIywdutPJp11YSGQXwM\n+nil4mTB/cBWHXlzcNzaBBoPc7s3+CE5s155fzKP4VSRLRu3zF6SdZ+go7jPP8GL\nnvf8ChBzt4VwJc4abreZkDn/q8FkCHN9dIQ8Yi4sFd9zs2WdkUhV/me9RZDCZjqZ\nOO4A0YtyHN9VIcgwidZWSBT3yWbwrgklGDq3RsMwK5RkIDbn81QCzG1nTOr2tEqz\nX8CmI60AAI/HHhuMWX8HmynDHzO7hCJ0egOei9G7ZU0Z8RNe45FjhSLcdIFCJYjM\n1FOEi693GDIg1oSMRs3F\n=jPr7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T08:47:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commit/b9713992480a1ee9eeae6964c52da6ce41c6adb8","node_id":"C_kwDOTVO3DtoAKGI5NzEzOTkyNDgwYTFlZTllZWFlNjk2NGM1MmRhNmNlNDFjNmFkYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commit/321fd5572968c40a7a7011ed028602db56e13887","sha":"321fd5572968c40a7a7011ed028602db56e13887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/321fd5572968c40a7a7011ed028602db56e13887"}],"sha":"b9713992480a1ee9eeae6964c52da6ce41c6adb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/b9713992480a1ee9eeae6964c52da6ce41c6adb8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104142635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zrmnelson","id":104142635,"login":"zrmnelson","node_id":"U_kgDOBjUXKw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/321fd5572968c40a7a7011ed028602db56e13887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:22:25Z","email":"104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zeno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:22:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MYAH-359: add manual Instagram message composer to the command menu (#163)\n\n* MYAH-359 Add manual Instagram message composer to the command menu\n\nAdds a separate global \"Message on Instagram\" command and a durable\nside-panel composer for manual first messages and for exact messages\ninto an existing conversation, with immutable approvals and receipts,\nexact Inbox projection, rolling action budgets and no automatic resend.\n\nIncludes the safety work the feature depends on: Unipile messaging\nidentity contracts, v3 immutable snapshots, read-only account/recipient\nroute preparation, frozen one-click attempts, receipt-first recovery,\nverified projection and reconciliation, and the 2.20 upgrade commands\nthat synchronize the composer command and search metadata.\n\nAlso fixes two defects found during isolated local UAT and independent\npre-PR review:\n\n- An existing conversation this workspace had not synced yet failed\n  closed as \"ambiguous\". Resolution now materialises the verified local\n  conversation on demand and never resurrects an operator-deleted one.\n- A receipt that was never dispatched was swept to UNKNOWN and could\n  never be resolved, permanently locking that recipient for both the\n  composer and the Inbox. It now settles to FAILED and releases its\n  target claim, which is safe because the dispatch marker is committed\n  before the provider write is issued.\n\n* MYAH-359: regenerate SDK metadata client and fix dormant budget-test seed\n\n- Regenerate packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/{schema.graphql,schema.ts}\n  to add MESSAGE_ON_INSTAGRAM to EngineComponentKey, matching the command\n  registered by this branch. Caught by CI''s server-validation codegen-drift\n  check, which could only run once the merge conflicts were resolved.\n- Fix instagram-action-budget.integration-spec.ts''s insertProcessingReceipt\n  seed helper: it never set actionKind on the raw actionApprovalBinding\n  INSERT, which has required actionKind IN (''START_CHAT'',''REPLY'') since\n  before this branch or MYAH-354 existed (confirmed byte-identical fixture\n  on origin/main). Dormant bug, only now exercised because this branch is\n  the first to make this integration spec file ''affected'' under Nx''s\n  test-scoping. Sets actionKind: ''REPLY'', matching the reservation seed\n  helper''s hardcoded kind for these same tests.\n\n* MYAH-359: renumber composer metadata upgrade commands to real timestamps\n\nMYAH-354 (PR #161) already merged to main with newer 2.20.0 command\ntimestamps (...748001/2/3) than this branch''s SynchronizeInstagramComposerMetadataCommand\n(1789488000360) and its paired AddInstagramMessageV3SnapshotFastInstanceCommand\n(1789488000359), which were authored before #161 existed. CI''s\n''keep the sequence append-only'' guard correctly flagged this: our commands''\nstale timestamps sort before commands already live on main, which could move\nthe upgrade cursor backwards for any workspace that already applied #161.\n\nRenumber both to real, current timestamps after #161''s max\n(1789633748003 -> 1789633748004 for the fast-instance command,\n1789633748005 for the workspace command). Safe because neither command\nhas ever shipped or run on any workspace under its old name -- this is\nnot the ''renumber an already-applied migration'' case the append-only\nguard and this repo''s history are otherwise careful to avoid.\n\nUpdates all cross-references (filenames, imports, decorator timestamps,\ndurable-name assertions) and the final-sequence/kind-window assertions in\n2-20-upgrade-version-command.module.spec.ts, which now also needs to\nexclude MYAH-354''s two triage workspace commands and its fast-instance\ntriage-mode command from the Instagram-only cutover-window accounting,\nsince the renumbering widened that window past them.\n\n* MYAH-359: extract and compile missing Lingui locale catalogs\n\nThe Instagram composer''s new UI strings (SidePanelInstagramMessagePage,\nInstagramMessageRecipientInput, MessageOnInstagramCommand, etc.) were\nnever run through ''lingui extract''/''lingui compile'' before the original\ncommit, so the .po catalogs and their compiled generated/*.ts output were\nstale. CI''s ''Verify Lingui catalog outputs'' step (front-sb-build job)\ncorrectly caught this: it re-runs extract+compile and fails if that\nproduces any diff.\n\nThis was misdiagnosed in an earlier pass as a runner-memory/OOM issue on\nthe storybook build step, based on skimming raw log text; the GitHub\nActions job-steps API makes clear the actual failing step is ''Verify\nLingui catalog outputs'', which runs and fails *before* the storybook\nbuild step (which was only ever skipped as a consequence, not itself\nbroken). Re-running extract+compile locally reproduces the exact same\ndiff and is idempotent on a second run.\n\n* MYAH-359: fix react-router-dom mock breaking pre-existing Campaign tests\n\nRoot cause found after deep bisection (previous ''pre-existing bug'' claim\nwas wrong and is retracted): the true original test file (from MYAH-338/\nMYAH-354, verified against commit 52303536 and origin/main tip b5010988,\nboth of which pass this file 19/19) never mocked react-router-dom''s\nuseNavigate. This branch added a file-wide\n\n    jest.mock(''react-router-dom'', () => ({\n      ...jest.requireActual(''react-router-dom''),\n      useNavigate: () => mockInstagramNavigate,\n    }))\n\nto the same shared test file for the new Instagram composer tests. Because\njest.mock applies file-wide, this silently broke the two pre-existing\nCampaign-guidance tests further down the file, which depend on real\nMemoryRouter navigation to reach the Campaign route and back.\n\nConfirmed via bisection: removing every other diff between this branch''s\ntest file and the true original (setup() signature, composer imports/\ncomponent, new composer test cases) still left the 2 Campaign tests\nfailing; restoring the original no-op useNavigate mock''s real delegation\nwas the only change that fixed them, with a reconstructed tree combining\nmain''s tip with only this branch''s relevant files.\n\nFix: keep mockInstagramNavigate as a recording jest.fn() (so the composer\ntests'' assertions on it keep working) but delegate to the real navigate\nfunction via jest.requireActual, so real MemoryRouter navigation keeps\nworking for the Campaign tests. Verified 23/23 in this file, plus every\nother test file touching MyahInboxPage/the Instagram composer (unaffected).\n\nSupersedes and retracts the MYAH-397 ''pre-existing dormant bug'' framing:\nthis was a real regression from this branch''s own test changes, not a\ndormant defect on main.","tree":{"sha":"453ddb3941b5fd1e8b72e115ffe8e72959498ae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/git/trees/453ddb3941b5fd1e8b72e115ffe8e72959498ae5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/git/commits/321fd5572968c40a7a7011ed028602db56e13887","verification":{"payload":"tree 453ddb3941b5fd1e8b72e115ffe8e72959498ae5\nparent b79b75af81f8409757929335224a5b3a2b2bc551\nauthor zeno <104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com> 1789888945 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789888945 +0530\n\nMYAH-359: add manual Instagram message composer to the command menu (#163)\n\n* MYAH-359 Add manual Instagram message composer to the command menu\n\nAdds a separate global \"Message on Instagram\" command and a durable\nside-panel composer for manual first messages and for exact messages\ninto an existing conversation, with immutable approvals and receipts,\nexact Inbox projection, rolling action budgets and no automatic resend.\n\nIncludes the safety work the feature depends on: Unipile messaging\nidentity contracts, v3 immutable snapshots, read-only account/recipient\nroute preparation, frozen one-click attempts, receipt-first recovery,\nverified projection and reconciliation, and the 2.20 upgrade commands\nthat synchronize the composer command and search metadata.\n\nAlso fixes two defects found during isolated local UAT and independent\npre-PR review:\n\n- An existing conversation this workspace had not synced yet failed\n  closed as \"ambiguous\". Resolution now materialises the verified local\n  conversation on demand and never resurrects an operator-deleted one.\n- A receipt that was never dispatched was swept to UNKNOWN and could\n  never be resolved, permanently locking that recipient for both the\n  composer and the Inbox. It now settles to FAILED and releases its\n  target claim, which is safe because the dispatch marker is committed\n  before the provider write is issued.\n\n* MYAH-359: regenerate SDK metadata client and fix dormant budget-test seed\n\n- Regenerate packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/{schema.graphql,schema.ts}\n  to add MESSAGE_ON_INSTAGRAM to EngineComponentKey, matching the command\n  registered by this branch. Caught by CI''s server-validation codegen-drift\n  check, which could only run once the merge conflicts were resolved.\n- Fix instagram-action-budget.integration-spec.ts''s insertProcessingReceipt\n  seed helper: it never set actionKind on the raw actionApprovalBinding\n  INSERT, which has required actionKind IN (''START_CHAT'',''REPLY'') since\n  before this branch or MYAH-354 existed (confirmed byte-identical fixture\n  on origin/main). Dormant bug, only now exercised because this branch is\n  the first to make this integration spec file ''affected'' under Nx''s\n  test-scoping. Sets actionKind: ''REPLY'', matching the reservation seed\n  helper''s hardcoded kind for these same tests.\n\n* MYAH-359: renumber composer metadata upgrade commands to real timestamps\n\nMYAH-354 (PR #161) already merged to main with newer 2.20.0 command\ntimestamps (...748001/2/3) than this branch''s SynchronizeInstagramComposerMetadataCommand\n(1789488000360) and its paired AddInstagramMessageV3SnapshotFastInstanceCommand\n(1789488000359), which were authored before #161 existed. CI''s\n''keep the sequence append-only'' guard correctly flagged this: our commands''\nstale timestamps sort before commands already live on main, which could move\nthe upgrade cursor backwards for any workspace that already applied #161.\n\nRenumber both to real, current timestamps after #161''s max\n(1789633748003 -> 1789633748004 for the fast-instance command,\n1789633748005 for the workspace command). Safe because neither command\nhas ever shipped or run on any workspace under its old name -- this is\nnot the ''renumber an already-applied migration'' case the append-only\nguard and this repo''s history are otherwise careful to avoid.\n\nUpdates all cross-references (filenames, imports, decorator timestamps,\ndurable-name assertions) and the final-sequence/kind-window assertions in\n2-20-upgrade-version-command.module.spec.ts, which now also needs to\nexclude MYAH-354''s two triage workspace commands and its fast-instance\ntriage-mode command from the Instagram-only cutover-window accounting,\nsince the renumbering widened that window past them.\n\n* MYAH-359: extract and compile missing Lingui locale catalogs\n\nThe Instagram composer''s new UI strings (SidePanelInstagramMessagePage,\nInstagramMessageRecipientInput, MessageOnInstagramCommand, etc.) were\nnever run through ''lingui extract''/''lingui compile'' before the original\ncommit, so the .po catalogs and their compiled generated/*.ts output were\nstale. CI''s ''Verify Lingui catalog outputs'' step (front-sb-build job)\ncorrectly caught this: it re-runs extract+compile and fails if that\nproduces any diff.\n\nThis was misdiagnosed in an earlier pass as a runner-memory/OOM issue on\nthe storybook build step, based on skimming raw log text; the GitHub\nActions job-steps API makes clear the actual failing step is ''Verify\nLingui catalog outputs'', which runs and fails *before* the storybook\nbuild step (which was only ever skipped as a consequence, not itself\nbroken). Re-running extract+compile locally reproduces the exact same\ndiff and is idempotent on a second run.\n\n* MYAH-359: fix react-router-dom mock breaking pre-existing Campaign tests\n\nRoot cause found after deep bisection (previous ''pre-existing bug'' claim\nwas wrong and is retracted): the true original test file (from MYAH-338/\nMYAH-354, verified against commit 52303536 and origin/main tip b5010988,\nboth of which pass this file 19/19) never mocked react-router-dom''s\nuseNavigate. This branch added a file-wide\n\n    jest.mock(''react-router-dom'', () => ({\n      ...jest.requireActual(''react-router-dom''),\n      useNavigate: () => mockInstagramNavigate,\n    }))\n\nto the same shared test file for the new Instagram composer tests. Because\njest.mock applies file-wide, this silently broke the two pre-existing\nCampaign-guidance tests further down the file, which depend on real\nMemoryRouter navigation to reach the Campaign route and back.\n\nConfirmed via bisection: removing every other diff between this branch''s\ntest file and the true original (setup() signature, composer imports/\ncomponent, new composer test cases) still left the 2 Campaign tests\nfailing; restoring the original no-op useNavigate mock''s real delegation\nwas the only change that fixed them, with a reconstructed tree combining\nmain''s tip with only this branch''s relevant files.\n\nFix: keep mockInstagramNavigate as a recording jest.fn() (so the composer\ntests'' assertions on it keep working) but delegate to the real navigate\nfunction via jest.requireActual, so real MemoryRouter navigation keeps\nworking for the Campaign tests. Verified 23/23 in this file, plus every\nother test file touching MyahInboxPage/the Instagram composer (unaffected).\n\nSupersedes and retracts the MYAH-397 ''pre-existing dormant bug'' framing:\nthis was a real regression from this branch''s own test changes, not a\ndormant defect on main.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr4mxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOmUQADsJCa7gfwn9x/AP4HVIalWY\nBxgtdvFHAWYfzjOVeeknjisC9avYYNB5oLlXSYoOK28ObhVB64YzsmtD/+RdAYxS\nsjKaLprFWquLSmbuHci3H5GUr2ZmqNmWUUn5b0zF5m5m8uVXpBSnViHaoPW//Uwg\neqNXZLFiwae75A+nxClK2O66obxcjG/cLlZ81097umzuqCvnSGin6YZ9B8ja1Oyt\nV55f0wK7hHFdCW++XPm3TW1gvMuSC1+Qrb6R6rTI4ffaOvLcGvGg33ARtLeIpOGj\nYMBnsR9dTYdow7cTkMFPFfJ01IkRy6SYdgz9CK8DI3UongCDEoEd61PZ80WEhkCL\nuK8p/PhfaGv44FR6mAqxdzvOYnngIteBBHqvskkk7PbuNvpyfrmEK1GEDv32ZfTG\naaoZBfVPXVkx38UrRUiZB05+TzNXg4IiX32ZPtra17WOqVpxTZwSz7aqmq50nY8k\n+Dy2d1qLObL8VjPir9lC6C8AMYD6ZRPqePSRGqVXM8qqUGWr4A3/JpXVfb4fZW+n\nPU2pCEkPtRL2shtAqHbPAVWIkZe2WD1K2xuT6Wu2iKuGKA1lJqkkcZwx2XPDZQC0\naQYZdlKclxOE9KoZR972OJDYQtnCNFEJczv8kZCgfXuYaQ9su0IRG/YCVUAOJ38d\n+PmYV7pDWKv/4HL9F7EQ\n=8PpW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:22:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"