users/deestax/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/deestax","id":152369481,"login":"deestax","node_id":"U_kgDOCRT5SQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deestax","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commit/32abdff55a5718d1c39add76cea89c81fbd69359","node_id":"C_kwDOTVO3DtoAKDMyYWJkZmY1NWE1NzE4ZDFjMzlhZGQ3NmNlYTg5YzgxZmJkNjkzNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commit/b5010988870aca752891547c5e0b98f4cd3fc88c","sha":"b5010988870aca752891547c5e0b98f4cd3fc88c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/b5010988870aca752891547c5e0b98f4cd3fc88c"}],"sha":"32abdff55a5718d1c39add76cea89c81fbd69359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/32abdff55a5718d1c39add76cea89c81fbd69359"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104142635?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zrmnelson","id":104142635,"login":"zrmnelson","node_id":"U_kgDOBjUXKw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zrmnelson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commits/b5010988870aca752891547c5e0b98f4cd3fc88c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:14:08Z","email":"104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zeno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T06:14:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MYAH-354: make Inbox triage state contact-wide across Email and Instagram (#161)\n\n* feat(inbox): make triage state contact-wide across Email and Instagram\n\nAdds one authoritative Owner/State/Snooze tuple per Inbox contact, replacing\nper-thread and per-channel triage.\n\n- Private per-workspace tables for the contact identity, triage tuple,\n  transition receipts, Email channel provenance and migration marker, with their\n  indexes. They are deliberately not exposed as workspace objects, metadata,\n  GraphQL, search, pickers, workflows, or automation.\n- Capability-gated reads, filters, counts and mutations. Owner projection is\n  permission-aware, and expected capability or missing-metadata failures collapse\n  to a single generic unavailable response. Mutations use revision plus identity\n  generation compare-and-set and return typed, sanitized conflicts.\n- Live readable inbound Email or Instagram evidence sets Needs reply, clears\n  snooze and preserves owner. Replay and history are ordered and deduplicated.\n  Outbound and Campaign activity preserve state. Expired snoozes project as\n  Needs reply without a scheduler.\n- Link, unlink, Creator update/delete/merge and generic source mutations\n  reconcile whole tuples under a single global lock order (migration marker,\n  sorted Creator anchors and source locks, source rows, then sorted identity and\n  triage locks). Stale linked source contact IDs are rejected under source locks\n  before shared Creator tuple locking.\n- Migration installs capture before baseline, treats pre-baseline producer tuples\n  as provisional, atomically replaces them from approved legacy precedence,\n  fences the baseline, catches up to stability, then marks READY. Valid\n  Email-only workspaces omit absent optional Instagram app relations, and runtime\n  code never creates app-owned tables. In-flight Email import progress stays owned\n  by the existing cache-based pending-cursor mechanism (MYAH-387); this change\n  does not introduce a second source of truth for it.\n- The three new 2.20 commands use fresh timestamps so they do not collide with\n  SynchronizeCampaignLifecycleStatusMetadataCommand.\n- Frontend Owner/State/Snooze controls live in the shared contact header with\n  concurrency tokens, unavailable and conflict handling, and due-snooze refresh.\n\n* fix(inbox): close review findings on contact-wide triage cutover\n\nResolves the independent review of the contact-wide triage change set.\n\n- Critical: the polling import path now forwards the triage source boundary\n  (BACKFILL for a channel''s first import, LIVE after a completed sync, plus the\n  in-flight generation owned by the pending-cursor cache). Without it the normal\n  inbound Email path persisted messages without transition receipts, so new\n  inbound mail never reopened or refreshed a contact. Covered by a regression\n  test that fails against the previous call site.\n- Remove the remaining legacy per-thread triage surface to finish the documented\n  cutover: the thread summary no longer projects state/snoozedUntil/inboxOwner,\n  the thread query drops its owner/state/snooze filters, the thread mutation\n  keeps only Creator and Campaign relinking, agent tools stop advertising thread\n  triage, and the frontend stops reading or rendering it. Legacy columns stay\n  physically present and unused.\n- Snooze contract: a deadline supplied for any non-Snoozed state is cleared\n  server-side instead of rejected, and an invalid Snoozed deadline raises a\n  validation error instead of an internal failure.\n- Receipt recovery isolates failures per workspace so one unprovisioned schema\n  cannot abort the sweep.\n- Contact reads preflight the private triage relations and fail closed with the\n  generic response during a partial upgrade instead of surfacing a raw SQL error.\n  The probe bypasses datasource permission checks, which the PostgreSQL suites\n  caught while it was missing.\n- Bound the outer contact page plan assertion on the page LIMIT itself rather\n  than on one planner shape.\n\nVerified: PostgreSQL myah-inbox and upgrade suites 82/82, affected server unit\nunion green, frontend 1076 suites / 6904 tests, tsgo and lint/format clean for\nboth packages, and a live UAT smoke (contact reads, cross-channel tuple, typed\nMYAH_INBOX_TRIAGE_CONFLICT, thread query without triage filters).\n\n* fix(inbox): keep message persistence independent of the triage schema\n\nResolves the second review round''s blocking finding: making the polling\nimport pass triage source evidence also made every inbound Email batch\ndepend on the private triage schema, because the migration-marker lock runs\nbefore message persistence in the same transaction. A workspace whose\nprivate relations are not provisioned yet (for example a worker that starts\nwhile the 2.20 command is still running) would then fail the whole batch with\n`42P01`, persist nothing, and mark the channel failed for the relaunch window.\n\nThe triage schema is now probed before any triage write, and absence means\n\"no triage\" rather than a failed import:\n\n- MyahInboxContactTriageReceiptService.isTriageSchemaProvisioned checks the\n  migration marker with to_regclass (the marker is written last, so absence\n  proves the private schema is missing).\n- lockMigrationMarkerForSourcePersistenceInTransaction returns false when the\n  schema is absent, and recordInTransaction then skips receipt recording.\n- MessagingSaveMessagesAndEnqueueContactCreationService keeps persisting\n  messages with no source lock, no receipts and no tuple work in that case.\n- The Instagram projection skips its receipt and tuple continuations too.\n\nNothing is lost while the schema is absent: the migration baseline derives\ninbound ordering evidence from persisted messages, not from receipts.\n\nAlso updates the agent-tool spec, which still drove `inboxState` through a\ntool that no longer accepts it, and now asserts that triage fields are\nrejected at the tool schema boundary.\n\nVerified: affected server union 209 suites / 2266 tests (one cwd-dependent\nspec passes under nx test, 4/4), PostgreSQL myah-inbox + upgrade 82/82,\nserver tsgo and lint/format clean, server build, and a live UAT smoke.\n\n* fix(inbox): align assistant instructions and cover the absent-schema projection\n\nCloses the two small items the third review round recorded as follow-ups to\nthe schema-probe fix.\n\n- The seeded Myah Inbox assistant skill still told the assistant to change\n  thread state by calling update_myah_inbox_thread, which no longer accepts\n  triage fields and whose description says so. The instruction now states that\n  Owner, State and Snooze are contact-wide and cannot be changed by these\n  tools, and keeps the approval requirement for the Creator/Campaign relink\n  that the tool does support.\n- The Instagram projection''s absent-schema branch had no test: it now has one\n  asserting that the conversation and message rows are still written while\n  neither receipt recording nor tuple initialisation runs.\n\nVerified: affected server union 236 suites / 2467 tests (the single reported\nfailure is the cwd-dependent render spec, 4/4 under nx test), server tsgo and\nlint/format clean.\n\n* fix(inbox): provision triage schema in CI fixtures, skip upgrade on missing data source\n\nTwo real CI-only bugs caught by the full GitHub Actions matrix but missed\nby locally-scoped test runs:\n\n- Pre-existing integration specs extended to touch contact-wide triage\n  (task-7, reply-proposal, contact-projection, mutation, assistant-skills)\n  never provisioned the private triage tables, because CI''s integration\n  shards reset+seed the DB but don''t run the 2.20 upgrade. Added an\n  idempotent ensureMyahInboxContactTriageTables test util (reuses the\n  schema service''s own DDL/marker logic) and wired it into the shared\n  Task 7 fixture and the mutation spec''s beforeAll.\n\n- InitializeMyahInboxContactTriageWorkspaceCommand and\n  CatchUpMyahInboxContactTriageWorkspaceCommand threw when a workspace\n  had no data source, aborting the entire cross-version upgrade run for\n  every other workspace. Every sibling 2.20 workspace command instead\n  skips and returns; aligned both commands with that pattern and added\n  unit coverage for the skip path.","tree":{"sha":"aa2156df5f3071142004d3565d13f18aaab13621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/git/trees/aa2156df5f3071142004d3565d13f18aaab13621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/git/commits/b5010988870aca752891547c5e0b98f4cd3fc88c","verification":{"payload":"tree aa2156df5f3071142004d3565d13f18aaab13621\nparent 2eeae2ff0dcb4578012e49e32ccef45914f06d8a\nauthor zeno <104142635+zrmnelson@users.noreply.github.com> 1789712048 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789712048 +0530\n\nMYAH-354: make Inbox triage state contact-wide across Email and Instagram (#161)\n\n* feat(inbox): make triage state contact-wide across Email and Instagram\n\nAdds one authoritative Owner/State/Snooze tuple per Inbox contact, replacing\nper-thread and per-channel triage.\n\n- Private per-workspace tables for the contact identity, triage tuple,\n  transition receipts, Email channel provenance and migration marker, with their\n  indexes. They are deliberately not exposed as workspace objects, metadata,\n  GraphQL, search, pickers, workflows, or automation.\n- Capability-gated reads, filters, counts and mutations. Owner projection is\n  permission-aware, and expected capability or missing-metadata failures collapse\n  to a single generic unavailable response. Mutations use revision plus identity\n  generation compare-and-set and return typed, sanitized conflicts.\n- Live readable inbound Email or Instagram evidence sets Needs reply, clears\n  snooze and preserves owner. Replay and history are ordered and deduplicated.\n  Outbound and Campaign activity preserve state. Expired snoozes project as\n  Needs reply without a scheduler.\n- Link, unlink, Creator update/delete/merge and generic source mutations\n  reconcile whole tuples under a single global lock order (migration marker,\n  sorted Creator anchors and source locks, source rows, then sorted identity and\n  triage locks). Stale linked source contact IDs are rejected under source locks\n  before shared Creator tuple locking.\n- Migration installs capture before baseline, treats pre-baseline producer tuples\n  as provisional, atomically replaces them from approved legacy precedence,\n  fences the baseline, catches up to stability, then marks READY. Valid\n  Email-only workspaces omit absent optional Instagram app relations, and runtime\n  code never creates app-owned tables. In-flight Email import progress stays owned\n  by the existing cache-based pending-cursor mechanism (MYAH-387); this change\n  does not introduce a second source of truth for it.\n- The three new 2.20 commands use fresh timestamps so they do not collide with\n  SynchronizeCampaignLifecycleStatusMetadataCommand.\n- Frontend Owner/State/Snooze controls live in the shared contact header with\n  concurrency tokens, unavailable and conflict handling, and due-snooze refresh.\n\n* fix(inbox): close review findings on contact-wide triage cutover\n\nResolves the independent review of the contact-wide triage change set.\n\n- Critical: the polling import path now forwards the triage source boundary\n  (BACKFILL for a channel''s first import, LIVE after a completed sync, plus the\n  in-flight generation owned by the pending-cursor cache). Without it the normal\n  inbound Email path persisted messages without transition receipts, so new\n  inbound mail never reopened or refreshed a contact. Covered by a regression\n  test that fails against the previous call site.\n- Remove the remaining legacy per-thread triage surface to finish the documented\n  cutover: the thread summary no longer projects state/snoozedUntil/inboxOwner,\n  the thread query drops its owner/state/snooze filters, the thread mutation\n  keeps only Creator and Campaign relinking, agent tools stop advertising thread\n  triage, and the frontend stops reading or rendering it. Legacy columns stay\n  physically present and unused.\n- Snooze contract: a deadline supplied for any non-Snoozed state is cleared\n  server-side instead of rejected, and an invalid Snoozed deadline raises a\n  validation error instead of an internal failure.\n- Receipt recovery isolates failures per workspace so one unprovisioned schema\n  cannot abort the sweep.\n- Contact reads preflight the private triage relations and fail closed with the\n  generic response during a partial upgrade instead of surfacing a raw SQL error.\n  The probe bypasses datasource permission checks, which the PostgreSQL suites\n  caught while it was missing.\n- Bound the outer contact page plan assertion on the page LIMIT itself rather\n  than on one planner shape.\n\nVerified: PostgreSQL myah-inbox and upgrade suites 82/82, affected server unit\nunion green, frontend 1076 suites / 6904 tests, tsgo and lint/format clean for\nboth packages, and a live UAT smoke (contact reads, cross-channel tuple, typed\nMYAH_INBOX_TRIAGE_CONFLICT, thread query without triage filters).\n\n* fix(inbox): keep message persistence independent of the triage schema\n\nResolves the second review round''s blocking finding: making the polling\nimport pass triage source evidence also made every inbound Email batch\ndepend on the private triage schema, because the migration-marker lock runs\nbefore message persistence in the same transaction. A workspace whose\nprivate relations are not provisioned yet (for example a worker that starts\nwhile the 2.20 command is still running) would then fail the whole batch with\n`42P01`, persist nothing, and mark the channel failed for the relaunch window.\n\nThe triage schema is now probed before any triage write, and absence means\n\"no triage\" rather than a failed import:\n\n- MyahInboxContactTriageReceiptService.isTriageSchemaProvisioned checks the\n  migration marker with to_regclass (the marker is written last, so absence\n  proves the private schema is missing).\n- lockMigrationMarkerForSourcePersistenceInTransaction returns false when the\n  schema is absent, and recordInTransaction then skips receipt recording.\n- MessagingSaveMessagesAndEnqueueContactCreationService keeps persisting\n  messages with no source lock, no receipts and no tuple work in that case.\n- The Instagram projection skips its receipt and tuple continuations too.\n\nNothing is lost while the schema is absent: the migration baseline derives\ninbound ordering evidence from persisted messages, not from receipts.\n\nAlso updates the agent-tool spec, which still drove `inboxState` through a\ntool that no longer accepts it, and now asserts that triage fields are\nrejected at the tool schema boundary.\n\nVerified: affected server union 209 suites / 2266 tests (one cwd-dependent\nspec passes under nx test, 4/4), PostgreSQL myah-inbox + upgrade 82/82,\nserver tsgo and lint/format clean, server build, and a live UAT smoke.\n\n* fix(inbox): align assistant instructions and cover the absent-schema projection\n\nCloses the two small items the third review round recorded as follow-ups to\nthe schema-probe fix.\n\n- The seeded Myah Inbox assistant skill still told the assistant to change\n  thread state by calling update_myah_inbox_thread, which no longer accepts\n  triage fields and whose description says so. The instruction now states that\n  Owner, State and Snooze are contact-wide and cannot be changed by these\n  tools, and keeps the approval requirement for the Creator/Campaign relink\n  that the tool does support.\n- The Instagram projection''s absent-schema branch had no test: it now has one\n  asserting that the conversation and message rows are still written while\n  neither receipt recording nor tuple initialisation runs.\n\nVerified: affected server union 236 suites / 2467 tests (the single reported\nfailure is the cwd-dependent render spec, 4/4 under nx test), server tsgo and\nlint/format clean.\n\n* fix(inbox): provision triage schema in CI fixtures, skip upgrade on missing data source\n\nTwo real CI-only bugs caught by the full GitHub Actions matrix but missed\nby locally-scoped test runs:\n\n- Pre-existing integration specs extended to touch contact-wide triage\n  (task-7, reply-proposal, contact-projection, mutation, assistant-skills)\n  never provisioned the private triage tables, because CI''s integration\n  shards reset+seed the DB but don''t run the 2.20 upgrade. Added an\n  idempotent ensureMyahInboxContactTriageTables test util (reuses the\n  schema service''s own DDL/marker logic) and wired it into the shared\n  Task 7 fixture and the mutation spec''s beforeAll.\n\n- InitializeMyahInboxContactTriageWorkspaceCommand and\n  CatchUpMyahInboxContactTriageWorkspaceCommand threw when a workspace\n  had no data source, aborting the entire cross-version upgrade run for\n  every other workspace. Every sibling 2.20 workspace command instead\n  skips and returns; aligned both commands with that pattern and added\n  unit coverage for the skip path.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrNawCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd2wQAFKrQKR+fiu8t3YbhcJhAYOG\nKDaMEzFiDeD/PPCx1lbDkM/FtZK70XwEk6JgDRdIJNH56aivq8ZkTY1+C7UBtasv\nLzClCGG5rwZAAx35JMbO1Bv7XUx/8Kz13n6mFwXsK19ajiqoLZIbgrrmevY+VVm/\nMbaB9SCY4xOU0P7/IEkflm1KCnD8Qm20//dply92Zi1OLQUVGfo+ckZvwqdkPKQh\nxxH26RKQAZDXq3E2aGZx0CJToZKsCgu5OAsm+O7+LZUYbhWA1myTp3bRYJ+3K7I0\naq0RnD0TNXKDZF+gg9NqyP2GLd7e6Aa9y5hsw9MVVdZreJk6hdvthf29yqn41CSb\n6QWOsWryzDSUCjSzpxQa6L5RPQt0YFyV1loX2GYlqMrzYlPkfwxyTCeUQp8giF0y\noysQAgE8LyxBM7OUIRIzB4KNGDX82xNbEuEgGzYjwLMab2Hn8QO8JJsqqHadom34\nfNwcb73qFd07Lm395j6Afpu25FAE8mpWH4ONw+0iMmiJh69owJfigPfj146X/D/E\nQA5OUVYSlcoByIBJXkPpMaepaCe0sAhydsxqfgkplwgY54PXcbPpHlSRMPyKS8tp\nU5oDUAJQJbChHaKgjQMxd4toF5V3UTUICUh7b9OH1Wt6MDjW1VVCf+ZyI4aSbUOr\nAsaYZ/OuQT0FfDEKNAUu\n=u4KN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T06:14:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/T3-Venture-Labs-Limited/myah-v4/commit/b5010988870aca752891547c5e0b98f4cd3fc88c","node_id":"C_kwDOTVO3DtoAKGI1MDEwOTg4ODcwYWNhNzUyODkxNTQ3YzVlMGI5OGY0Y2Q