xZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kk-harmony/WordGameBff/commit/9c8a624470f7d8e22040e7747c4b092b316b9414","sha":"9c8a624470f7d8e22040e7747c4b092b316b9414","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kk-harmony/WordGameBff/commits/9c8a624470f7d8e22040e7747c4b092b316b9414"}],"sha":"b60126f258a6a79326aee68ad4ff4096f28291f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kk-harmony/WordGameBff/commits/b60126f258a6a79326aee68ad4ff4096f28291f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148013352?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kk-harmony","id":148013352,"login":"kk-harmony","node_id":"U_kgDOCNKBKA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kk-harmony","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kk-harmony/WordGameBff/commits/9c8a624470f7d8e22040e7747c4b092b316b9414/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:57:27Z","email":"148013352+kk-harmony@users.noreply.github.com","name":"kiran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:57:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Redis SignalR backplane, session lobbies, and party-scale UX (#1)\n\n* Replace Postgres NOTIFY backplane with Equinoctial Redis pub/sub.\n\nFixes intermittent missed SignalR fanout on long-lived Fly machines by switching to Redis with local dispatch, revision dedup, lightweight notify payloads, and targeted per-instance fanout.\n\n* Add Podman Redis preflight with optional 2-node cluster.\n\nReuse host Redis when reachable; otherwise start redis-1/redis-2 for the local SignalR backplane and shift demo/BFF host ports to avoid common clashes.\n\n* Offset local host ports and share defaults across Podman and CI.\n\nAvoid clashes with other stacks by moving BFF/demo/playground/embed to 8180/3100/5174/8083, centralize defaults in local-dev-ports.sh, and harden managed Redis health checks via host ports.\n\n* Raise rate limits and enable snapshot push for party games.\n\nShared-NAT tables were hitting auth/api IP caps; run auth before the limiter so session quotas key on sub.\n\n* Turn off upstream Quarkus rate limits in CI compose.\n\nBFF owns client rate limiting; hermetic stacks no longer need raised Bucket4j permits.\n\n* Ease ~15-player play with safer home UX and lighter PoW.\n\nSplit home into Player/Admin tabs (join by default), allow admins to leave a waiting room, raise auth throughput, and drop PoW to 16 bits so shared-NAT tables can start without accidental creates or long auth stalls.\n\n* Add session lobby proxy with 5-character join codes end-to-end.\n\nAdmins share a durable session ID across games; BFF/UI/SDK and Nepali copy follow the new flow, with TDD coverage and Cursor rules for SOLID/i18n.\n\n* Show session scores after finish and let admin start the next game.\n\nSurface cumulative member scores on the finished screen, keep polling the lobby so players auto-join the next round, and cover the flow in SDK/BFF/i18n/e2e tests.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: kiran <kk-harmony@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"597146cffb815a40a428f8f863057ce7fc4b249a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kk-harmony/WordGameBff/git/trees/597146cffb815a40a428f8f863057ce7fc4b249a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kk-harmony/WordGameBff/git/commits/9c8a624470f7d8e22040e7747c4b092b316b9414","verification":{"payload":"tree 597146cffb815a40a428f8f863057ce7fc4b249a\nparent 65cbf4a15c0afbdc7536dcb1c91ee2dab0200a95\nauthor kiran <148013352+kk-harmony@users.noreply.github.com> 1790657847 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790657847 -0500\n\nRedis SignalR backplane, session lobbies, and party-scale UX (#1)\n\n* Replace Postgres NOTIFY backplane with Equinoctial Redis pub/sub.\n\nFixes intermittent missed SignalR fanout on long-lived Fly machines by switching to Redis with local dispatch, revision dedup, lightweight notify payloads, and targeted per-instance fanout.\n\n* Add Podman Redis preflight with optional 2-node cluster.\n\nReuse host Redis when reachable; otherwise start redis-1/redis-2 for the local SignalR backplane and shift demo/BFF host ports to avoid common clashes.\n\n* Offset local host ports and share defaults across Podman and CI.\n\nAvoid clashes with other stacks by moving BFF/demo/playground/embed to 8180/3100/5174/8083, centralize defaults in local-dev-ports.sh, and harden managed Redis health checks via host ports.\n\n* Raise rate limits and enable snapshot push for party games.\n\nShared-NAT tables were hitting auth/api IP caps; run auth before the limiter so session quotas key on sub.\n\n* Turn off upstream Quarkus rate limits in CI compose.\n\nBFF owns client rate limiting; hermetic stacks no longer need raised Bucket4j permits.\n\n* Ease ~15-player play with safer home UX and lighter PoW.\n\nSplit home into Player/Admin tabs (join by default), allow admins to leave a waiting room, raise auth throughput, and drop PoW to 16 bits so shared-NAT tables can start without accidental creates or long auth stalls.\n\n* Add session lobby proxy with 5-character join codes end-to-end.\n\nAdmins share a durable session ID across games; BFF/UI/SDK and Nepali copy follow the new flow, with TDD coverage and Cursor rules for SOLID/i18n.\n\n* Show session scores after finish and let admin start the next game.\n\nSurface cumulative member scores on the finished screen, keep polling the lobby so players auto-join the next round, and cover the flow in SDK/BFF/i18n/e2e tests.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: kiran <kk-harmony@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu0U3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPWkQABjmbW46roQTmlHfzrBavtCT\n7FCAnsskvPhoseOPSoRyji/9NLguQzvzehzPHhW0Nwl4AaQDU7zHDL2v/gQT9Xsn\nn31H3qOc91MulV5gcXHD0mo/jHyOxm8g3epdce/8kP4tJkxFKXezYwJ8VHk4BlwR\nv70mLZ87L5NpWuZrlCY2ZfHtftkJi7TDgYDN6IAZj21Mwb/p3oWqnbME4JgJHaXn\ng5B7W8R1kdp55LFkraLqV+cPjzkw8ZBUOc/DWFb5eM4dJu5hHNe4HV4uZ8rZVhCE\nwkTuiLZQI6Z1YRjqnCUeIw/E5UfLAsOflFYJPX/i5dXcV/mFeIm+92OZcErjC4IU\n++aQYPgYTlLG7+vc7UDgsLlRTXgGU6FV6sxqqB+1glFT5LtgU2dWyUzaHySFtYM+\nUNN3iBxvk1wtG7FxBFiJSsqm2WFX0J7OIyq+wiDfMLHoJmpiCDJnFsl05lr8CT+G\n/5k/s248qVJM5/jDYdXI+yeckkQEU/4NUg9Cv6YeWuettOnwMvuyHCTToFigf0E9\nNF9WXl0uMHzWkQussXdDXAch1bI88kExs7wfaeg/F+4M4txc1Lujn1mutz9JTD+r\nFgQr1zOiDJqVCKNYwKm2XYUxqrUf+Yfog7tfcfKCtGDl1kctVWz+VemRgiZorhmw\n1i2xC9ocZgYAGHxWngI0\n=HKqB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T04:57:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https