 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"101e631ffc9756c5d4f4aa21cd711ced5ff07045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/101e631ffc9756c5d4f4aa21cd711ced5ff07045"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/b099115ef6c8ad1a6442c0ed92c27cdd2e88a18a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/b099115ef6c8ad1a6442c0ed92c27cdd2e88a18a","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKGIwOTkxMTVlZjZjOGFkMWE2NDQyYzBlZDkyYzI3Y2RkMmU4OGExOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64","sha":"c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64"}],"sha":"b099115ef6c8ad1a6442c0ed92c27cdd2e88a18a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/b099115ef6c8ad1a6442c0ed92c27cdd2e88a18a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:00:02Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T03:00:02Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Align headless launch with Playwright: automation flags, old --headless, CDP pipe transport\n\nCuts headless Chrome''s process count and resident memory toward Playwright''s\nby matching its automation-default launch flags and transport.\n\nLaunch flags (crates/cdp/src/launch.rs): headless launches now carry\nPlaywright''s automation-default flag set (HEADLESS_AUTOMATION_FLAGS) on top of\nthe existing reduction flags -- the big process/RSS wins being\n--disable-features=... (kills background service processes),\n--disable-component-extensions-with-background-pages, --disable-breakpad,\n--disable-sync, --metrics-recording-only, --no-service-autorun. Measured in a\nLinux container against the same chromium: process tree ~8-10 (was ~15) and\n~696 MB (was ~972 MB). Every default stays overridable/removable via the\nexisting --chrome-arg / [browser].extra_args / TRUEWRIGHT_CHROME_ARGS sources,\nwhich are appended last (Chrome''s last-flag-wins).\n\nHeadless mode: full-Chrome headless now uses old --headless instead of\n--headless=new; --headless=new is opt-in via --chrome-arg=--headless=new.\n(On Chrome 132+ old headless was removed, so the two are equivalent there --\nthe genuinely light headless path remains chrome-headless-shell, still\npreferred by default.)\n\nCDP transport: on Unix the launch now speaks CDP over --remote-debugging-pipe\n(inherited fds 3/4, NUL-delimited JSON) instead of a TCP loopback debugging\nport -- no port to allocate/scan and no DevToolsActivePort poll, removing the\n\"timed out attaching to browser devtools endpoint\" flakiness seen in\nsandboxed/container environments and shaving the ~700ms port-wait off cold\nstart. New PipeTransport (crates/cdp/src/transport.rs) plugs into the existing\nTransport seam; launch wires two pipes and dup2s their child ends onto fds 3/4\nin pre_exec (alongside the existing setsid). Windows and an\nTRUEWRIGHT_CDP_TRANSPORT=websocket escape hatch keep the TCP/WebSocket path.\nLaunchedBrowser now exposes its endpoint via Browser::connect_launched rather\nthan a raw ws_url field.\n\ndoctor: reports tree_process_count alongside tree_rss_mb (the direct signal for\nthe flag reductions), in both text and JSON.\n\nVerified on Linux/chromium in Docker: full cdp+engine browser suite passes over\nthe pipe transport; process count 8-10; all flags present on the spawned\ncommand line and overridable. The absolute RSS/cold-start/per-op head-to-head\nagainst Playwright should be re-run on the target LXC, since those numbers are\nhardware/environment specific.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e6913bca633ef6e8777a43654dc2b69bcb0516d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/9e6913bca633ef6e8777a43654dc2b69bcb0516d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKGMzMGMyZTViMmI1YTQ5OTkwZTQzNmY1YmM2ZDAwZDk2NTMxNDhhNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4","sha":"58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4"}],"sha":"c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/c30c2e5b2b5a49990e436f5bc6d00d9653148a64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T01:39:04Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T01:39:04Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Add configurable Chrome launch flags, container/CI --no-sandbox, and `truewright update`; bump to 0.0.4\n\nExtra Chrome/Edge launch flags can now be supplied to `mcp`, `doctor`,\nand `agent` from three cumulative sources: a repeatable `--chrome-arg`\nCLI option, a `[browser].extra_args` config list, and the\n`TRUEWRIGHT_CHROME_ARGS` environment variable. The env var is read at the\nlaunch layer (cdp), so it reaches every entry point -- including the test\nsuite -- without threading; config + CLI flags are threaded through\nengine `Session::launch_with_args` and `TruewrightTools::with_chrome_args`.\nThis unblocks unprivileged LXC/CI (`--no-sandbox`) and gives the\nlive-view its streamed look (`--kiosk`, window size/position).\n\n--no-sandbox is now auto-applied on Linux not just as root but also\ninside a container or under CI (detected via the `container`/`CI` env\nvars and the `/.dockerenv` / `/run/.containerenv` markers), de-duplicated\nagainst an explicitly-supplied one. A `--no-sandbox` CLI shortcut on all\nthree commands forces it when detection misses (e.g. an unprivileged\nLXC that sets none of those signals).\n\n`truewright update` is a new subcommand that execs the `truewright-update`\ncompanion binary installed alongside it, forwarding args -- a stable\nalias for an auto-update timer. Source/other installs with no companion\nget a clear message.\n\n`truewright doctor` now prints a visible line while the managed\nchrome-headless-shell downloads on a cold cache (the download logs only\nat info level, below doctor''s default warn filter, so a first run\nlooked like it hung), and surfaces the reason on fallback/failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00cc3a2457c7bae002c1647cbb61e39a1b569061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/00cc3a2457c7bae002c1647cbb61e39a1b569061"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKDU4YzVhOTY1NTdhMmJlNzljNWFiMjVkNGQ1M2MwOTdmZWFmNzg3YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334","sha":"f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334"}],"sha":"58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/58c5a96557a2be79c5ab25d4d53c097feaf787a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T05:55:49Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T05:55:49Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Add a native right-click primitive across all layers; bump to 0.0.3\n\nRight-click had no first-class support: agents could only left-click,\nso a page''s own context menu was unreachable. This threads a right\n(secondary) button through every input layer, mirroring the existing\nclick path exactly and differing only in the dispatched button:\n\n- cdp: Page::right_click_at (CDP button \"right\", which fires a native\n  contextmenu) and os_input right_click_at / walk_and_right_click\n  (SendInput MOUSEEVENTF_RIGHTDOWN/UP) for true_input.\n- engine: Session::right_click / right_click_with, sharing click''s\n  dispatch via a new MouseButton param -- so human_like motion,\n  trained profiles, seeds, and true_input all work identically.\n- mcp: browser_right_click tool with the same RefRequest shape as\n  browser_click.\n- yaml: a `right_click: ref` step that round-trips through export.\n- agent: a right_click tool in the browser_run_task loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f2a3cd09e817cb033e66447b80067d34814ea050","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/f2a3cd09e817cb033e66447b80067d34814ea050"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKGY1OGRkOTNjY2U5OWZmOGY3Y2YzNWYwYmJkZDdlZTJmMjdiZDAzMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd","sha":"a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd"}],"sha":"f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/f58dd93cce99ff8f7cf35f0bbdd7ee2f27bd0334"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T16:54:40Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T16:54:40Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Add --version and a self-update companion binary; bump to 0.0.2\n\nCli now derives --version (clap''s version attribute wasn''t set, so\nit errored on an unexpectedly-named argument instead of printing\nanything) -- needed so an update mechanism has something to compare\nagainst the latest GitHub release tag.\n\ndist-workspace.toml gains install-updater = true: the shell/\npowershell installers now also drop a small truewright-update\nbinary (via cargo-dist''s axoupdater) alongside the app for anyone\ninstalling that way. This machine''s own existing git-clone install\npredates that path, so it gets an equivalent update check via a\nseparate PowerShell script + Scheduled Task instead of switching it\nover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8900cc826ad12f01d3142cd4cf5cc63c233c5783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/8900cc826ad12f01d3142cd4cf5cc63c233c5783"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKGE4OTRkYjk1Y2Q1N2QwNTJkNmZjMmRjZTY2MDM0NWM1NTgxZjViY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d","sha":"56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d"}],"sha":"a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/a894db95cd57d052d6fc2dce660345c5581f5bcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T16:28:02Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T16:28:02Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Fix stdio MCP mode sharing one Chrome profile across concurrent processes\n\nEvery stdio `truewright mcp` process used the same fixed profile\nname (\"truewright-mcp\"), so multiple concurrent instances -- e.g.\none MCP host spawning a subprocess per open conversation window --\nraced for the same Chrome user-data directory. Only whichever\nprocess grabbed it first could actually launch/drive a working\nbrowser; the rest failed or hung (reproduced live: a second stdio\nprocess attempting browser_navigate timed out attaching to the\nDevTools endpoint while an existing process already held that\nprofile).\n\nsrc/mcp.rs''s stdio run() now generates a random per-process suffix\nand calls with_profile_name directly, the same mechanism router()\nalready used correctly for streamable-HTTP sessions (mcp-streamable-\nhttp spec: \"Independent per-session browser\") -- stdio just never\ngot the equivalent treatment, since it looked like a \"one process,\none profile\" case from a single terminal, which doesn''t hold once a\nhost can spawn more than one concurrent subprocess.\nwith_browser_pref''s fixed-name behavior is preserved as an explicit\nsingle-process debug/test convenience, just no longer what the real\nentry point uses.\n\nVerified by reproducing the original failure (two concurrent stdio\nsubprocesses via a minimal Python MCP client, second one timing out)\nand then confirming the fix resolves it (both processes independently\nlaunch and navigate without collision). Full workspace suite green\n(two unrelated environmental flakes during a from-scratch run --\nconsole_capture_flow and network_flow -- both confirmed by isolated\nre-run to be pre-existing resource-contention sensitivity on a\nmachine already under heavy load from the stale processes this fix\naddresses, not caused by this change, which touches none of that\ncode).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5af8a8b066ac6afdaf351d51ab7d32e292bbd5a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/5af8a8b066ac6afdaf351d51ab7d32e292bbd5a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKDU2ZDdjMmIzZWU3ZjJjMmIwNTZhNjgzZjhmYzJiYWY5ZjI1NWI1MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f","sha":"f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f"}],"sha":"56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/56d7c2b3ee7f2c2b056a683f8fc2baf9f255b52d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T10:36:12Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T10:36:12Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Add cross-platform release automation via cargo-dist\n\ngit tag vX.Y.Z && git push --tags now triggers .github/workflows/\nrelease.yml (generated by `dist init`/`dist generate`, not\nhand-written -- future changes should go through `dist generate`\nrather than editing the workflow directly): builds truewright for\nLinux/macOS (x86_64 + aarch64) and Windows x86_64, generates a\nshell and a PowerShell install script (curl/irm one-liners for a\nhuman or an agent to fetch a working binary with no Rust toolchain\nrequired), and publishes everything to a GitHub Release with\nchecksums.\n\nCargo.toml gains repository/description/readme (dist errors without\na valid repository URL) and the [profile.dist] release profile dist\nitself adds. Verified via `dist plan`, which produces the expected\nartifact set for the current v0.0.1 without actually cutting a\nrelease.\n\nAlso closes a gap noticed while reviewing what''s public on GitHub:\n.claude/settings.local.json and .claude/scheduled_tasks.lock were\nonly ever excluded by Claude Code''s own global gitignore, not this\nrepo''s -- added to .gitignore directly so that''s not\nrepo-config-dependent. No secrets were ever present in them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"49a2f69853d738423bcd4574fe934516752c5d94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/49a2f69853d738423bcd4574fe934516752c5d94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKGY5N2IyNWFlYzVmYzA2ZDllNzFkYjEyMjNmZjM2MzA4NmJmZGMwMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc","sha":"4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc"}],"sha":"f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/f97b25aec5fc06d9e71db1223ff363086bfdc00f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T10:05:17Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T10:05:17Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Rename project from ai-browser/aib to Truewright\n\nRenames the binary/package (aib -> truewright), the AibTools MCP\nserver struct (-> TruewrightTools), env vars (AIB_CONFIG ->\nTRUEWRIGHT_CONFIG, AIB_CHROME_PATH -> TRUEWRIGHT_CHROME_PATH), the\nper-user data directory (<LOCALAPPDATA>/aib -> .../truewright), the\ninjected-JS namespace globals (window.__aib -> window.__truewright,\nand its __aibTrain/__aibSuppressTraining/__aibAdvanceClock\nsiblings), default profile/cassette/skill naming, and every live\ndoc/prose reference across README.md, PROPOSAL.md, the current\nopenspec/specs/* capability specs, and doc comments -- scoped to\n\"live\" content only. openspec/changes/archive/** and .research/**\nare left untouched, matching this project''s own precedent of not\nrewriting historical records (like git history) after the fact.\n\nPackage/binary rename regenerates Cargo.lock; verified the compiled\ntruewright.exe runs with correct --help text, and the renamed data\ndirectory correctly re-downloads chrome-headless-shell on first use\n(one transient parallel-download-race failure during verification,\nconfirmed by isolated re-run to be the same category of resource\ncontention this project has already documented elsewhere, not a\nrename defect). Full workspace suite and clippy green (one\nunrelated, separately-confirmed-flaky true_input_flow failure\nduring the full parallel run, passing in isolation both before and\nafter this change).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cc9a14250e6d7bc86861ba9453dd38bc3561fe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/0cc9a14250e6d7bc86861ba9453dd38bc3561fe8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKDRmYzYyNjIyMzExMTE4YjdhMmY2M2EzZjgxZjZiMmMyMTliOGViZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a","sha":"75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a"}],"sha":"4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/4fc62622311118b7a2f63a3f81f6b2c219b8ebdc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T07:15:48Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T07:15:48Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Sync mcp-task-delegation spec into main tree and archive the change\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"699e6ec8aa76f205d73e1373329564fc1be35517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/699e6ec8aa76f205d73e1373329564fc1be35517"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKDc1YmQwMjhlOThhZDE2ZTkxMjQ3OTNlOTMxMTA3ODM1YjRjMmZhOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6","sha":"36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6"}],"sha":"75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/75bd028e98ad16e9124793e931107835b4c2fa8a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T07:15:05Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T07:15:05Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Implement mcp-task-delegation: browser_run_task + screenshot vision-interpret\n\nNew browser_run_task(task, guidance?, skills?, max_steps?) MCP tool\nruns the configured driver role''s agent loop over the same\nengine::Session every other browser_* tool on the server already\nshares, so an outer MCP host can delegate a whole sub-task and keep\ndriving the same live browser afterward. A failed task is a\ntool-level error result carrying the step transcript, matching how\nbrowser_assert already reports failure. browser_screenshot and\nbrowser_record_stop''s preview frame gain optional interpret/guidance\nparams routing the image through Harness::interpret_image and\nreturning text instead, for a host model with no vision of its own\n-- purely additive, omitting them keeps today''s exact image-returning\nbehavior.\n\nAibTools gains an optional agent: Option<AgentConfig> (harness +\nskill search dirs, bundled together since they''re only ever\nmeaningful as a pair) via a new .with_agent(...) builder rather than\na constructor parameter, so every existing constructor and call site\nis untouched by a field that''s None in the common (no LLM\nconfigured) case. Client/CompatClient/ResponsesClient/RoleClient/\nHarness gain #[derive(Clone)] so browser_run_task can build a\nper-call Harness with its own lower default max_steps (25, vs the\nCLI''s config-driven default) without threading a new parameter\nthrough Harness::run_task or touching change 3''s existing call\nsites/tests.\n\naib mcp gains --config; src/mcp.rs''s run/router/run_http thread the\noptional AgentConfig through to each AibTools. A config file that\nfails to parse warns to stderr; simply having no [roles.driver]\nconfigured stays silent, the same zero-LLM-setup guarantee every\nother aib subcommand already makes.\n\nVerified against a real Chrome session and real local LLM stubs\n(new tests/support/llm_stub.rs) over a real streamable-HTTP MCP\nclient: a full browser_run_task pass, the session surviving a\ndelegated task for further ordinary tool calls afterward, no driver\nconfigured failing as a clear protocol error, and screenshot\ninterpretation returning text from a real second vision stub. Plus a\nmanual end-to-end smoke test of the compiled aib mcp --http binary\nagainst a real separate-process Python LLM stub and real headless\nChrome, driven by raw curl MCP requests. Suite green on host and in\nthe Docker container.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87f1094eb506033388bd5e6d6299c11f0e201141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/87f1094eb506033388bd5e6d6299c11f0e201141"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKDM2Y2VlZjM0OTdlMjRlZTk1ZDIwZTRiOGJmNDJmZTMyYmE3MzM4YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485","sha":"e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485"}],"sha":"36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/36ceef3497e24ee95d20e4b8bf42fe32ba7338c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T07:14:42Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T07:14:42Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Propose mcp-task-delegation: browser_run_task + screenshot vision-interpret\n\nFourth and last of four agent-harness changes: the browser MCP\nserver gains browser_run_task so an outer MCP host can delegate a\nwhole sub-task to aib''s own configured driver over the same shared\nsession, and browser_screenshot/browser_record_stop gain an optional\ninterpret mode returning vision-model text for vision-less outer\nmodels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a712bd111306c1e7eb99092d9fec227046f52c10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/a712bd111306c1e7eb99092d9fec227046f52c10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr","id":2134382,"login":"leonjvr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQzODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485","node_id":"C_kwDOTWAagNoAKGUzMmUzYTAyZDgzNzgxYjQxNGJlNTkxYjJhZjE5MjAzNDE4NDQ0ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leonjvr/truewright/commit/552a9a0ffe09c8b4a0f9a7c4e92c89ed4cd2e8f0","sha":"552a9a0ffe09c8b4a0f9a7c4e92c89ed4cd2e8f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/552a9a0ffe09c8b4a0f9a7c4e92c89ed4cd2e8f0"}],"sha":"e32e3a02d83781b414be591b2af1920341844485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/e3