":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/commits/4cba294194d7e5fc64c510858d201bd23002e5b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T22:06:24Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T22:06:24Z","email":"ljradicals@gmail.com","name":"Leon Janse van Rensburg"},"message":"Add research review: continue ai-browser, re-prioritize efficiency + video\n\nVerifies .research/High Performance Browser Automation.md claim by claim:\nLightpanda is real but cannot screenshot (disqualifying for a testing\ntool), OxyBlink does not appear to exist, and the doc''s central insight --\nthe browser binary dominates cost, not the driver -- is correct and\nconsistent with our own measurements. Recommendation: continue; insert\nbrowser-efficiency and screencast-capture phases ahead of human motion,\nand relax the zero-download principle for headless runs (auto-downloaded\nchrome-headless-shell, installed-Chrome fallback).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b9121ef26e0982569e0c59961632cfca78b2d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/trees/5b9121ef26e0982569e0c59961632cfca78b2d62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leonjvr/truewright/git/commits/4cba294194d7e5fc64c510858d201bd23002e5b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2134382?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonjvr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.