44764557afd84399a341f7c86","node_id":"C_kwDOTWbLTtoAKGIwZGM2MzdkYmQzZWE4NzQ0NzY0NTU3YWZkODQzOTlhMzQxZjdjODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982","sha":"cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982"}],"sha":"b0dc637dbd3ea8744764557afd84399a341f7c86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/b0dc637dbd3ea8744764557afd84399a341f7c86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T17:18:53Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T17:18:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: test twenty-apps install against latest dockerhub and local server + new trigger (#22636)\n\n## Why\n\nApp installability can silently regress from two directions, and today\nCI only covers one of them:\n\n1. A **server** change (about to merge from the monorepo) breaks the\nability to install the **current public apps** — a\nbackward-compatibility regression users would hit on upgrade.\n2. An **app** change breaks against a server **built from the current\nmonorepo files** (not just the last published image), so the app and the\nupcoming server drift apart before either ships.\n\nBoth are compatibility guarantees between the server and the app\ncatalog. Today they are only tested from the app side, against the\nlatest published image. This PR makes CI enforce the contract from both\nsides:\n\n- Any server PR must keep **every** current public app installable.\n- Any app PR is exercised against both the **released** server (its\nintegration suite — what users run today) and the **upcoming**\n(monorepo) server (integration plus deploy + install).\n\n## What\n\nShared building blocks so both CIs exercise the same paths instead of\nduplicating them:\n\n- **`spawn-twenty-server`** (composite action) — returns a running\nserver (`server-url` + `api-key`) from either the latest published\nDocker Hub image or a server built from the monorepo. Both sources\nexpose the same contract, so callers never branch on how the server came\nup.\n- **`test-twenty-app`** (composite action) — exercises one app against a\ngiven server, delegating deploy + install to the shared\n`deploy-twenty-app` / `install-twenty-app` actions.\n- **`discover-apps`** (reusable workflow) — the single source of truth\nfor the app matrix. Parameterized by `scope` (`public` vs\n`internal-and-public`) and `changed-only`, so both CIs derive their\nmatrix from the filesystem instead of a hand-maintained list. Discovery\nstays automatic: a newly added public app is picked up with no CI edit,\nwhich is what keeps the \"every public app\" guarantee honest.\n\nWired in:\n\n- **CI Server** gains a `server-apps-install-smoke` matrix that installs\nevery public app (`discover-apps` with `scope: public, changed-only:\nfalse`) against the about-to-merge server, gated in\n`ci-server-status-check` so a regression blocks merge.\n- **CI Twenty Apps** discovers changed apps (`scope:\ninternal-and-public, changed-only: true`) and runs each against both\nserver sources — the released image and the monorepo build.\n\n## Why the coverage differs per side (not \"always everything\")\n\n`test-twenty-app` has three explicit modes —\n`installation-and-integration-test` (integration + deploy + install),\n`integration-test-only` (suite only), `installation-only` (deploy +\ninstall only) — because the useful signal depends on what actually\nchanged:\n\n- **App PR against the monorepo server →\n`installation-and-integration-test`.** The app changed, so run its whole\nsuite against the upcoming server, install included.\n- **App PR against the released server → `integration-test-only`.**\nChecks the app''s own suite against what users run today; install against\nthe released image is left to the SDK e2e path.\n- **Server PR → `installation-only`, across all apps.** The apps did not\nchange; the only question is \"can each one still be installed.\" Running\nevery app''s full integration suite on every server PR would be far\nslower and largely redundant. Installation-only keeps this broad (the\nwhole catalog) and cheap enough to always run and block merge.\n\nThe tradeoff is deliberate: broad but shallow where nothing in the app\nchanged, deep where it did.\n\n## Notes / trade-offs\n\n- On app-only PRs the `local` source pays a full server build per app\n(the `server-build` cache is only warm on server PRs). Could be\noptimized later with a shared warm-up job.\n- SDK-local (Verdaccio) install testing stays in\n`ci-create-app-e2e-minimal`; this PR''s `local` source targets the server\nbuild.\n\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22636?utm_source=github\"\nrel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">``&lt;img alt=\"Review\nin cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</a>","tree":{"sha":"49dd2d3077cd4f501c57d6ed418adb20ff392ed1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/trees/49dd2d3077cd4f501c57d6ed418adb20ff392ed1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/commits/cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982","verification":{"payload":"tree 49dd2d3077cd4f501c57d6ed418adb20ff392ed1\nparent 3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1783703933 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783703933 +0200\n\nci: test twenty-apps install against latest dockerhub and local server + new trigger (#22636)\n\n## Why\n\nApp installability can silently regress from two directions, and today\nCI only covers one of them:\n\n1. A **server** change (about to merge from the monorepo) breaks the\nability to install the **current public apps** — a\nbackward-compatibility regression users would hit on upgrade.\n2. An **app** change breaks against a server **built from the current\nmonorepo files** (not just the last published image), so the app and the\nupcoming server drift apart before either ships.\n\nBoth are compatibility guarantees between the server and the app\ncatalog. Today they are only tested from the app side, against the\nlatest published image. This PR makes CI enforce the contract from both\nsides:\n\n- Any server PR must keep **every** current public app installable.\n- Any app PR is exercised against both the **released** server (its\nintegration suite — what users run today) and the **upcoming**\n(monorepo) server (integration plus deploy + install).\n\n## What\n\nShared building blocks so both CIs exercise the same paths instead of\nduplicating them:\n\n- **`spawn-twenty-server`** (composite action) — returns a running\nserver (`server-url` + `api-key`) from either the latest published\nDocker Hub image or a server built from the monorepo. Both sources\nexpose the same contract, so callers never branch on how the server came\nup.\n- **`test-twenty-app`** (composite action) — exercises one app against a\ngiven server, delegating deploy + install to the shared\n`deploy-twenty-app` / `install-twenty-app` actions.\n- **`discover-apps`** (reusable workflow) — the single source of truth\nfor the app matrix. Parameterized by `scope` (`public` vs\n`internal-and-public`) and `changed-only`, so both CIs derive their\nmatrix from the filesystem instead of a hand-maintained list. Discovery\nstays automatic: a newly added public app is picked up with no CI edit,\nwhich is what keeps the \"every public app\" guarantee honest.\n\nWired in:\n\n- **CI Server** gains a `server-apps-install-smoke` matrix that installs\nevery public app (`discover-apps` with `scope: public, changed-only:\nfalse`) against the about-to-merge server, gated in\n`ci-server-status-check` so a regression blocks merge.\n- **CI Twenty Apps** discovers changed apps (`scope:\ninternal-and-public, changed-only: true`) and runs each against both\nserver sources — the released image and the monorepo build.\n\n## Why the coverage differs per side (not \"always everything\")\n\n`test-twenty-app` has three explicit modes —\n`installation-and-integration-test` (integration + deploy + install),\n`integration-test-only` (suite only), `installation-only` (deploy +\ninstall only) — because the useful signal depends on what actually\nchanged:\n\n- **App PR against the monorepo server →\n`installation-and-integration-test`.** The app changed, so run its whole\nsuite against the upcoming server, install included.\n- **App PR against the released server → `integration-test-only`.**\nChecks the app''s own suite against what users run today; install against\nthe released image is left to the SDK e2e path.\n- **Server PR → `installation-only`, across all apps.** The apps did not\nchange; the only question is \"can each one still be installed.\" Running\nevery app''s full integration suite on every server PR would be far\nslower and largely redundant. Installation-only keeps this broad (the\nwhole catalog) and cheap enough to always run and block merge.\n\nThe tradeoff is deliberate: broad but shallow where nothing in the app\nchanged, deep where it did.\n\n## Notes / trade-offs\n\n- On app-only PRs the `local` source pays a full server build per app\n(the `server-build` cache is only warm on server PRs). Could be\noptimized later with a shared warm-up job.\n- SDK-local (Verdaccio) install testing stays in\n`ci-create-app-e2e-minimal`; this PR''s `local` source targets the server\nbuild.\n\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22636?utm_source=github\"\nrel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">``&lt;img alt=\"Review\nin cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"&gt;``</a>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUSl9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALFwQAEbVo3YHwU6zAMu/zaqgKlIu\n0IeyG/AB3k80sR5wa6PE7hmC888z7qu3ZbO8djBSWV2emFytWnQRj+vUOH+qL0Jn\nT/M53Pr1v4E+e7/U+dt+R/ceFEvum/s3rK5APr3k1iiz2AhGNlw2ltzuSEVmaPUB\nPr1353BtNA+R7fQTIS7WGk+66iXF5EPTHVWx6ndP8VLSfaMon/L2rQr94cJTyJDl\nvhSf70GrV9a5JYGUph5GLEowZ9M2NSaxLHIVGPMAocHa9wHfwx0hqWdqxbOFScp3\nZM0/d5Nargs2R2Uvs3o26ZHxnEw0AIItpto6Nc/EWU9z+k1tjwjdaMQJWTC5J6PQ\nCeO98B2/oI2h/4l6zASjxTUWMrGdo/r/WPZMKEKwuaSmrFHE+OgRIcMG84eZcOL1\nYAcFJIpsZBG8i+1rLXvY5SILuxUwMXjLpXIarBlsSVSrSboDWP9doZ9XZ6yuC3p2\nA4ZMgsXeGD4W1G4ge1EEYceJuH8elrSS1FreLGD3kaYactIpWqNazNL/pFDXIbAU\nQZntnJlHyKAtqUakTCDb/uWsuD7gBZc1yqmfK3qNMr2IUw/t8qzYPTDjMSocrgQU\n6ZCeTREOcAhYy+CbCyRlhU7syrKPr3liQt5NNRQF/IiGxY0rHsLTHt0wz2dM+FNk\n6C/FbLFFQ2Xo0UyNzSsk\n=qHgx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T19:58:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982","node_id":"C_kwDOTWbLTtoAKGNiOTU0MTBhNTFmN2RlOTk0MTViMzQ3YTlkNTRkM2UzM2UxYTQ5ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1","sha":"3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1"}],"sha":"cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T16:33:25Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T16:33:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): stabilize app install version-gate integration test (#22826)\n\n## Why\n\nThe `failing-app-installation-workspace-version` integration suite fails\non CI (e.g. [this\nrun](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/actions/runs/29105697459/job/86405891168)):\n\n```\nApp requires Twenty server >=2.21.0 but this server is 2.20.0.\nsubCode: SERVER_VERSION_INCOMPATIBLE\n```\n\nThe test uploads an app requiring `>=${TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION}` and\nexpects the install to be rejected by the **workspace** version gate.\nBut after the `2.21.0` version bump, `TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION` (`2.21.0`)\nmoved ahead of the latest instance upgrade command (`2-20`, so\n`getInferredVersion()` returns `2.20.0`). The tarball upload runs the\n**instance** server-compat check first, which rejects `>=2.21.0` against\na `2.20.0` server before the workspace gate under test is ever reached.\n\nThe sibling sync test is unaffected because sync only validates\nworkspace compatibility, not the upload-time instance check.\n\n## What\n\nDerive the required version range from the version the instance actually\nreached (the workspace upgrade cursor via\n`extractVersionFromCommandName`) instead of the drifting\n`TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION` constant. This way:\n\n- The upload passes the instance server-compat check (server satisfies\n`>=<current version>`).\n- The workspace, which resolves one version behind after the injected\nfailed cursor, still fails the workspace gate, producing the expected\n`WORKSPACE_VERSION_INCOMPATIBLE` error.\n\nThe error assertion keeps using the normalized snapshot\n(`scrubSemverVersions`), so the concrete version numbers do not leak\ninto the snapshot and future version bumps won''t churn it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01XqhqQ8VGJZWBuznR8nRviX)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22826?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"42d6b5b3778728c221fd4f38658b11a47331033a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/trees/42d6b5b3778728c221fd4f38658b11a47331033a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/commits/3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1","verification":{"payload":"tree 42d6b5b3778728c221fd4f38658b11a47331033a\nparent c9d84ba7f074940b28760697d06139283dd35f5a\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1783701205 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783701205 +0000\n\nfix(server): stabilize app install version-gate integration test (#22826)\n\n## Why\n\nThe `failing-app-installation-workspace-version` integration suite fails\non CI (e.g. [this\nrun](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/actions/runs/29105697459/job/86405891168)):\n\n```\nApp requires Twenty server >=2.21.0 but this server is 2.20.0.\nsubCode: SERVER_VERSION_INCOMPATIBLE\n```\n\nThe test uploads an app requiring `>=${TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION}` and\nexpects the install to be rejected by the **workspace** version gate.\nBut after the `2.21.0` version bump, `TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION` (`2.21.0`)\nmoved ahead of the latest instance upgrade command (`2-20`, so\n`getInferredVersion()` returns `2.20.0`). The tarball upload runs the\n**instance** server-compat check first, which rejects `>=2.21.0` against\na `2.20.0` server before the workspace gate under test is ever reached.\n\nThe sibling sync test is unaffected because sync only validates\nworkspace compatibility, not the upload-time instance check.\n\n## What\n\nDerive the required version range from the version the instance actually\nreached (the workspace upgrade cursor via\n`extractVersionFromCommandName`) instead of the drifting\n`TWENTY_CURRENT_VERSION` constant. This way:\n\n- The upload passes the instance server-compat check (server satisfies\n`>=<current version>`).\n- The workspace, which resolves one version behind after the injected\nfailed cursor, still fails the workspace gate, producing the expected\n`WORKSPACE_VERSION_INCOMPATIBLE` error.\n\nThe error assertion keeps using the normalized snapshot\n(`scrubSemverVersions`), so the concrete version numbers do not leak\ninto the snapshot and future version bumps won''t churn it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01XqhqQ8VGJZWBuznR8nRviX)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22826?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUR7VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA06oQAGEDGwDa9xntZ9Yh6Um08VD+\nJirhvJb58qq1cALX7PX6pfL2JNj5AQCO9hguAaY+FTJgyQxBWaEMsfq+E+EEkErE\nGHPIRTQ7lDG9u2DzgqhltNjdeQzvzCUkQ8+GvNVPb53hA75En7Sg2rHkfkYFRA16\nKsZHniGFtavuGbLuQ10ob/2xJnRyf7kpxbLdi2Hzm87OFruuQtTXmlBb/HHzCyVP\nTmKDv7eOK+qc6ruIwUesrJYK4dxsljlhi8rasp5G7RQoL7IcVtZSKs5EwG2weAyD\n5XgEiDmIFv23DSHXwgc5QlL4IAy+EAGKji2YT3kkrASefePK1Hllpg20XMmUQ9pR\nYKbwqT5p8yyq0UQkr7ENLY84SivyPUipcNWhMdBiBK0nNu+F1Esx+kNKJWGGRygY\n6ILfrMDu7sL9+GpLH47Qr7TE/eMdIB8HZ+DbNB2W1/mz68A0ZC279gkZXethpt2T\nmzFdVOMMpPjQOYr5hT2k2euSumd/Fnh6vCXkPegHmjNUW65hhCA/qyjMxjV6dzOI\nKbhOUgF1B1OuFvQ8pU9tcrRuWFSCBmsszMQCsBfMeQbJWee3R9VHknbHwwVnQcC9\nHXIeE6gkdMhT5confXvyk5r30ZE3IzkUxvrFQHb8SdRnsRf6OgspQd5KIt9YasX5\nhnQA8KoiratudGhE6Lgn\n=wZZg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T19:58:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1","node_id":"C_kwDOTWbLTtoAKDM2MTQxODMyMDBlZTVhZGY0NGRhNWIxZGEwYmE1ZTI5OTY0MzVjYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/c9d84ba7f074940b28760697d06139283dd35f5a","sha":"c9d84ba7f074940b28760697d06139283dd35f5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/c9d84ba7f074940b28760697d06139283dd35f5a"}],"sha":"3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/3614183200ee5adf44da5b1da0ba5e2996435ca1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/c9d84ba7f074940b28760697d06139283dd35f5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:55:00Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T15:55:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Disable install button in app install onboarding when no app is selected (#22822)\n\nIn the app installation onboarding step, the Install button was always\nclickable, even with no app selected. Clicking it with an empty\nselection ran the completion flow with zero apps, which is equivalent to\nskipping.\n\nNow the button is disabled until at least one app is selected (in\naddition to staying disabled while completing). The Skip button remains\navailable for users who don''t want to install anything.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22822?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"cad284421af4971f6c6e634a5ae7a728411e205d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/trees/cad284421af4971f6c6e634a5ae7a728411e205d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/commits/c9d84ba7f074940b28760697d06139283dd35f5a","verification":{"payload":"tree cad284421af4971f6c6e634a5ae7a728411e205d\nparent c0f5a28d5d12b46fe2ed8ab85db2373fee671ec7\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1783698900 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783698900 +0200\n\nDisable install button in app install onboarding when no app is selected (#22822)\n\nIn the app installation onboarding step, the Install button was always\nclickable, even with no app selected. Clicking it with an empty\nselection ran the completion flow with zero apps, which is equivalent to\nskipping.\n\nNow the button is disabled until at least one app is selected (in\naddition to staying disabled while completing). The Skip button remains\navailable for users who don''t want to install anything.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22822?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqURXUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+KMQAGZ/HJrUEBlw8kv1/YjwiGW/\n/0vgq8MUsM2z7oAEEFCUq1PqNmE/gwgs9phXS6kx/fK3S0uolu6s5f9hC7vrQ1Pw\n5+Bm3H1l3vT+6GS0ZFIcFPp98VUKEm6x+0of2dfjoSAOjpvBXOTKvs80/ALnLW73\n3E01MqBj4Ap0MgBZSmmJExj2XGHZHQVCV3j6A8BaP76Hfs9d8oKCIJ4lrZcIlcCF\njbanNVg3THYlMl6/G+t2kuYdH1KQR/SDoNhZPqCaiyw+1KLqTmY7y9/CVndwXKwC\nK6lRYYcOxIVT57qp1zJXvHo7bFOCvbx1CxoODQ7+zap838fdSFZ6zzxYRLjKFoAX\nCxZhyPl4Tq9qZDxfx5veQD5ht2p2vF8yGaLV1iyl9cEBO9iDbiKIhchl9wmKg/h0\nhlF+Q6oKlbHs5OMofWt0Gnec+UxpFee6pzeWAZyi/Lldxrs7LRo+uyZzJVQSEgJD\nGMEauVZv82gopreOnxTHaHQkNTRrEV9gLVPiPAPn8iOHZzGgxKk1kkshU6OaEfWU\nAxR0xvXENjmiy+PtedNT0EDcdoIVR8wLk5hq4BcScgbJUgHXMIWWe30MFWJdqriK\nE+0fmjBIx6Hb4AjQoGz789aF+PbMF16WEkAaaJdn5Zk/AzG0fK8Xiig0PgFI8JV+\nn/CK/QzM5um/fpFjfKWo\n=ahDC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T19:58:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url"