19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/5f70beb2d267295fa8220d8cfc9020a128ae7fd5","node_id":"C_kwDOTWbLTtoAKDVmNzBiZWIyZDI2NzI5NWZhODIyMGQ4Y2ZjOTAyMGExMjhhZTdmZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/4fc3650b2d6919756076bdc1f7d205bcd2315d3b","sha":"4fc3650b2d6919756076bdc1f7d205bcd2315d3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/4fc3650b2d6919756076bdc1f7d205bcd2315d3b"}],"sha":"5f70beb2d267295fa8220d8cfc9020a128ae7fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/5f70beb2d267295fa8220d8cfc9020a128ae7fd5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/4fc3650b2d6919756076bdc1f7d205bcd2315d3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:16:33Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:16:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(emails): deterministic i18n catalog order to stop recurring i18n PR conflicts (#22803)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe automated `i18n - translations` PR (branch `i18n`) conflicts on\n`twenty-emails` `.po` files on **every** cycle. Each time, the msgid\n*set* is identical to main — only the entry **order** differs.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`twenty-emails` uses explicit message ids (`js-lingui-explicit-id`).\nWith lingui''s default ordering, **`lingui extract` is non-idempotent for\nthis catalog** — two consecutive runs on identical source produce\ndifferent `.po` orderings:\n\n```\n# no source change between runs\nlingui extract  # run 1\nlingui extract  # run 2  -> ~170 lines reordered vs run 1\n```\n\nSo the order produced by the `i18n-push` extract on main, the order\nstored in Crowdin, and the order the `i18n-pull` bot downloads never\nagree, and the translation PR re-conflicts perpetually.\n`twenty-front`/`twenty-server` use hashed ids and are already idempotent\n— this is isolated to emails.\n\n## Fix\n\nSet `orderBy: ''messageId''` in `twenty-emails/lingui.config.ts`. Verified\nthis makes extraction idempotent — two consecutive extracts now produce\nbyte-identical output.\n\nThis commit includes the one-time reorder of the existing catalogs into\nthe stable order. Generated `.ts` output is unchanged (already\norder-independent). After merge, one push cycle syncs Crowdin to the\nstable order, after which the recurring conflicts stop.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `nx run twenty-emails:lingui:extract` twice → no diff on the second\nrun.\n- `nx run twenty-emails:lingui:compile` → succeeds, generated `.ts`\nunchanged.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22803?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"934cd8966c1b95694056287982a4d8e092d1fb94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/trees/934cd8966c1b95694056287982a4d8e092d1fb94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/commits/4fc3650b2d6919756076bdc1f7d205bcd2315d3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 934cd8966c1b95694056287982a4d8e092d1fb94\nparent 945724e016d05744e73959c7dca80ff60efc9aba\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1783689393 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783689393 +0200\n\nfix(emails): deterministic i18n catalog order to stop recurring i18n PR conflicts (#22803)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe automated `i18n - translations` PR (branch `i18n`) conflicts on\n`twenty-emails` `.po` files on **every** cycle. Each time, the msgid\n*set* is identical to main — only the entry **order** differs.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`twenty-emails` uses explicit message ids (`js-lingui-explicit-id`).\nWith lingui''s default ordering, **`lingui extract` is non-idempotent for\nthis catalog** — two consecutive runs on identical source produce\ndifferent `.po` orderings:\n\n```\n# no source change between runs\nlingui extract  # run 1\nlingui extract  # run 2  -> ~170 lines reordered vs run 1\n```\n\nSo the order produced by the `i18n-push` extract on main, the order\nstored in Crowdin, and the order the `i18n-pull` bot downloads never\nagree, and the translation PR re-conflicts perpetually.\n`twenty-front`/`twenty-server` use hashed ids and are already idempotent\n— this is isolated to emails.\n\n## Fix\n\nSet `orderBy: ''messageId''` in `twenty-emails/lingui.config.ts`. Verified\nthis makes extraction idempotent — two consecutive extracts now produce\nbyte-identical output.\n\nThis commit includes the one-time reorder of the existing catalogs into\nthe stable order. Generated `.ts` output is unchanged (already\norder-independent). After merge, one push cycle syncs Crowdin to the\nstable order, after which the recurring conflicts stop.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `nx run twenty-emails:lingui:extract` twice → no diff on the second\nrun.\n- `nx run twenty-emails:lingui:compile` → succeeds, generated `.ts`\nunchanged.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22803?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reaso