url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/dcb67fbbe152c21439a5067577f37c0aa7afe6fd","node_id":"C_kwDOTWbLTtoAKGRjYjY3ZmJiZTE1MmMyMTQzOWE1MDY3NTc3ZjM3YzBhYTdhZmU2ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commit/bf1220883fef02ae6fcda037073e9ae3b2399f19","sha":"bf1220883fef02ae6fcda037073e9ae3b2399f19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/bf1220883fef02ae6fcda037073e9ae3b2399f19"}],"sha":"dcb67fbbe152c21439a5067577f37c0aa7afe6fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/dcb67fbbe152c21439a5067577f37c0aa7afe6fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11599358?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rashad","id":11599358,"login":"rashad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTk5MzU4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/bf1220883fef02ae6fcda037073e9ae3b2399f19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:39:31Z","email":"11599358+rashad@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rashad Karanouh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T12:39:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: partner CTAs on high-traffic pages (workflows, data-model, docker-compose) (#22808)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #22719 (merged), which added partner-marketplace CTAs to\nfour **high-intent, low-traffic** docs pages (SSO, both migration\nguides, implementation services).\n\nReviewing the docs'' **top-visited pages** showed none of those four rank\nin the top ~20 — they''re the high-intent tail, which is correct, but\nsmall reach. This PR extends the same pattern to three **high-traffic\npages that also carry buying intent**, without touching the pure\ntop-of-funnel intros/quickstarts (volume without intent → a CTA there is\njust noise).\n\nSame conventions as #22719: Mintlify-native `<Tip>` callouts,\npartner-first with `contact@twenty.com` secondary, directory deep-linked\nvia `?categories=<scope>` and tagged with `?ref=docs-*`. No new snippet;\nno `docs.json`, navigation, or translation (`l/`) changes.\n\n## Pages changed — screenshots (one per page)\n\n> Preview locally with `npx mintlify dev` from `packages/twenty-docs`,\nor use the Mintlify PR preview once it posts. Paths below are under\n`docs.twenty.com`.\n\n### 1. `/user-guide/workflows/overview` (~593 views)\nNew `## Need Help?` two-bullet `<Tip>` → **Done for you** (Solutioning\npartner) / **Onboarding pack** (Workflow Creation). Maps 1:1 to the\nnamed onboarding service.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"1440\" height=\"818\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-10 at 14 34 32\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/231f681d-b5be-4b1e-9b6a-a4947a9fca37\"\n/>\n\n\n### 2. `/user-guide/data-model/overview` (~954 views)\nReplaced the plain \"Need Help?\" line with a two-bullet `<Tip>` → **Done\nfor you** (Solutioning partner) / **Onboarding pack** (Data Model\nDesign). Keeps the existing Implementation Services link.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"1436\" height=\"817\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-10 at 14 34 14\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0fe1064-1030-4062-91c7-24644ac31654\"\n/>\n\n\n### 3. `/developers/self-host/capabilities/docker-compose` (~2421 views)\nNew `## Managed Hosting` single-line `<Tip>` → *find a certified Twenty\nhosting partner* (Hosting), contact fallback. Framed as a lighter\n\"prefer not to run it yourself?\" alternative — deliberately low-pressure\nfor the DIY self-host audience.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"1437\" height=\"815\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-10 at 14 33 39\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a37207cd-2aaa-4aba-848d-cbf06a1e1321\"\n/>\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Page-selection rationale: intent × volume. Kept the four intent-tail\npages from #22719; added the highest-traffic pages that also carry a\nnatural partner-buying moment (self-host → Hosting; workflows /\ndata-model → Solutioning). Intros/quickstarts/contribute pages\nintentionally left untouched.\n- **Attribution caveat (unchanged from #22719):** twenty.com''s analytics\n(Cloudflare Web Analytics) is path-based, so `?ref=` is not measurable\nyet. Per-page measurement via a `/go/*` redirect Worker remains a\nplanned, separate follow-up (out of scope here).\n- `mintlify validate` passes.\n\nOpened as a draft.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22808?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"eff48b2e932187f6760bc4483c386bf89005a6cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/trees/eff48b2e932187f6760bc4483c386bf89005a6cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/commits/bf1220883fef02ae6fcda037073e9ae3b2399f19","verification":{"payload":"tree eff48b2e932187f6760bc4483c386bf89005a6cb\nparent 55768cfe81a335aa4fa7ad4526df73bce2066c26\nauthor Rashad Karanouh <11599358+rashad@users.noreply.github.com> 1783687171 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783687171 +0200\n\ndocs: partner CTAs on high-traffic pages (workflows, data-model, docker-compose) (#22808)\n\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #22719 (merged), which added partner-marketplace CTAs to\nfour **high-intent, low-traffic** docs pages (SSO, both migration\nguides, implementation services).\n\nReviewing the docs'' **top-visited pages** showed none of those four rank\nin the top ~20 — they''re the high-intent tail, which is correct, but\nsmall reach. This PR extends the same pattern to three **high-traffic\npages that also carry buying intent**, without touching the pure\ntop-of-funnel intros/quickstarts (volume without intent → a CTA there is\njust noise).\n\nSame conventions as #22719: Mintlify-native `<Tip>` callouts,\npartner-first with `contact@twenty.com` secondary, directory deep-linked\nvia `?categories=<scope>` and tagged with `?ref=docs-*`. No new snippet;\nno `docs.json`, navigation, or translation (`l/`) changes.\n\n## Pages changed — screenshots (one per page)\n\n> Preview locally with `npx mintlify dev` from `packages/twenty-docs`,\nor use the Mintlify PR preview once it posts. Paths below are under\n`docs.twenty.com`.\n\n### 1. `/user-guide/workflows/overview` (~593 views)\nNew `## Need Help?` two-bullet `<Tip>` → **Done for you** (Solutioning\npartner) / **Onboarding pack** (Workflow Creation). Maps 1:1 to the\nnamed onboarding service.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"1440\" height=\"818\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-10 at 14 34 32\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/231f681d-b5be-4b1e-9b6a-a4947a9fca37\"\n/>\n\n\n### 2. `/user-guide/data-model/overview` (~954 views)\nReplaced the plain \"Need Help?\" line with a two-bullet `<Tip>` → **Done\nfor you** (Solutioning partner) / **Onboarding pack** (Data Model\nDesign). Keeps the existing Implementation Services link.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"1436\" height=\"817\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-10 at 14 34 14\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0fe1064-1030-4062-91c7-24644ac31654\"\n/>\n\n\n### 3. `/developers/self-host/capabilities/docker-compose` (~2421 views)\nNew `## Managed Hosting` single-line `<Tip>` → *find a certified Twenty\nhosting partner* (Hosting), contact fallback. Framed as a lighter\n\"prefer not to run it yourself?\" alternative — deliberately low-pressure\nfor the DIY self-host audience.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"1437\" height=\"815\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-10 at 14 33 39\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a37207cd-2aaa-4aba-848d-cbf06a1e1321\"\n/>\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Page-selection rationale: intent × volume. Kept the four intent-tail\npages from #22719; added the highest-traffic pages that also carry a\nnatural partner-buying moment (self-host → Hosting; workflows /\ndata-model → Solutioning). Intros/quickstarts/contribute pages\nintentionally left untouched.\n- **Attribution caveat (unchanged from #22719):** twenty.com''s analytics\n(Cloudflare Web Analytics) is path-based, so `?ref=` is not measurable\nyet. Per-page measurement via a `/go/*` redirect Worker remains a\nplanned, separate follow-up (out of scope here).\n- `mintlify validate` passes.\n\nOpened as a draft.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22808?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUOgDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAskwQAKGzewnkrw4MLSH+U3hy44i1\nZgqoeZgnHh85DKDxUXjSR0Rsd9LMDmAEFrJaFejmz08viNLyhBPoE/bvcybMpmZP\njoKbbNqu/rHbaw1okNvFkjySeHqVJ7hZ6w9N/M7GehTKrvU9BEEafQdcD7rs61PQ\nrdAX03mCF1BHs0jdgLOUNj/qovK2bnnridr074vpPZ5dnvPETxuVA+8egCqooCSm\nDzn43TvF5ZI1gIPeEEuHysump0mDnGPnCfgS+2F9XmGbNsx1l+95lpAlpJuDEj/Z\nSr/3crhmbaMpLecMRXHHiyry9xc6QAzkL5+4gQliBOGBkrdieVuKqcO8WaP1UH1y\n+ZwBSSurBYA1hJvIOPV5dut0DePpMHUKnq2Z5iLGsyJUdP37mRXqVULT6co7ympg\nbyOK2auquh5/pO5MVjR0GfghKrqr3eR+vnOUuwE7Gj+twu9tHheA7og+GnUhl5lj\nQcAfRIO7gD5nxguWsAtT9tIOA6+oIhHP6SWIrS6uVUHYV04TtNpvO7n8Cuxv7rgY\nLPYjNU1otdURdzAtofYl5ABmCEpAiMh9JY/X7mpnCpO/OcnryJr6waAs1trDngAi\nKfOeRO4UAkq/ZVCqGbDmyK9yKlMqDAuOh9ftllSF4FgbyF6a1uClVH2cpyCGH/Yh\nzcQMXd8LH7q4E+gyGdyh\n=i1RC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T19:58:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/eve