i.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/commits/ace16add6c086351c5d4909efd7cc403a551a272/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:27:21Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T11:27:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(twenty-partners): align createdAt view field with 2.19 deterministic ids and bump to 1.2.10 (#22782)\n\n## What\n\n- Bump `twenty-partners` from `1.2.0` to `1.2.10`.\n- Fix the red integration tests by pointing the \"Partner Applications\"\nview `createdAt` column at the real field metadata id.\n\n## Why the integration tests were red\n\nThe `twenty-partners` CI job spins up `twentycrm/twenty-app-dev:latest`\nand runs the integration suite. The suite''s global setup does a dev sync\nof the app, which failed:\n\n```\nDev sync failed: viewField: INVALID_VIEW_DATA: Field metadata not found\n(universalIdentifier: 835c9a7e-72ec-46c5-8d90-39a02998f561)\n```\n\nThe `partner-applications.view.ts` `createdAt` column referenced\n`PARTNER_CREATED_AT_FIELD_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER = 421cbcea-...`, an\ninvented id. `createdAt` is a reserved system field auto-created on the\ncustom `partner` object, and since 2.19 its universal identifier is\nderived deterministically by the server from the application id, the\nobject id and the field name. The invented id matched nothing, so the\nsync rejected the dangling view field and the app never registered,\nfailing every integration test.\n\n## Fix\n\nSet `PARTNER_CREATED_AT_FIELD_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER` to the\ndeterministically derived value `746e2944-28d0-545e-9832-a46516e1d9a0`\n(application id `e662fc1f-...` + partner object id `39101b39-...` +\nfield name `createdAt`). This matches the same derivation the server\nuses for standard object system fields, verified against the\n`twenty-shared` opportunity `createdAt` snapshot.","tree":{"sha":"ad37c9f4761b2e378601377d3c3f43a5a5272a65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/trees/ad37c9f4761b2e378601377d3c3f43a5a5272a65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AndresMarulanda10/odelza-platform/git/commits/ace16add6c086351c5d4909efd7cc403a551a272","verification":{"payload":"tree ad37c9f4761b2e378601377d3c3f43a5a5272a65\nparent 48252d35e91be5af4d3e42cf5d527646d62c8d87\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1783682841 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783682841 +0200\n\nfix(twenty-partners): align createdAt view field with 2.19 deterministic ids and bump to 1.2.10 (#22782)\n\n## What\n\n- Bump `twenty-partners` from `1.2.0` to `1.2.10`.\n- Fix the red integration tests by pointing the \"Partner Applications\"\nview `createdAt` column at the real field metadata id.\n\n## Why the integration tests were red\n\nThe `twenty-partners` CI job spins up `twentycrm/twenty-app-dev:latest`\nand runs the integration suite. The suite''s global setup does a dev sync\nof the app, which failed:\n\n```\nDev sync failed: viewField: INVALID_VIEW_DATA: Field metadata not found\n(universalIdentifier: 835c9a7e-72ec-46c5-8d90-39a02998f561)\n```\n\nThe `partner-applications.view.ts` `createdAt` column referenced\n`PARTNER_CREATED_AT_FIELD_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER = 421cbcea-...`, an\ninvented id. `createdAt` is a reserved system field auto-created on the\ncustom `partner` object, and since 2.19 its universal identifier is\nderived deterministically by the server from the application id, the\nobject id and the field name. The invented id matched nothing, so the\nsync rejected the dangling view field and the app never registered,\nfailing every integration test.\n\n## Fix\n\nSet `PARTNER_CREATED_AT_FIELD_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER` to the\ndeterministically derived value `746e2944-28d0-545e-9832-a46516e1d9a0`\n(application id `e662fc1f-...` + partner object id `39101b39-...` +\nfield name `createdAt`). This matches the same derivation the server\nuses for standard object system fields, verified against the\n`twenty-shared` opportunity `createdAt` snapshot.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUNcZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPocQAFHh/xTAEuWmOu8WE5Slm2Ck\nPPhz5owi2a3Y0ztvLlQwCPimNl8b+qubii77BnrqfNwpMdkpUMNOZoVekgdLS+U3\nbRRscQ5JzGZyQvABFaU2XuukYJCxsk2tMNITT0Yyp7qsyxLGpUrtJhLGTF4pav0p\nQq7xb9S38v41cNzz315bQX0fMGK131WKIOj1NPO0DyCYy7RfYgnAtF6a32cyx8af\nO6Jq4+fP2h2hthEWRxDzel7crGsCwal4lJs9ywrq3H9+uAr+LJw5VSncfuFO6v0Y\nyt1nG9SSBk7xm2DUmK3P29jnbybZjLnW5VKgdoxzxIGo5PKzqOUIuRWJ1uSemDfl\nanhDRJDBpUd8+D3EdFf8oYmybuLdJG9oxotdX7PuS7bNXDOnrDDmOH7vPl1HbvT5\nJFAUNFD/hVTCtxOuhKQrdITPMt2T0YsuC+E9gVwsCvLCtAINGnTyrwZMXuhtg7zo\ntzKyQNq/v9PdCkJij8ptgaXoQ9BmfF8b4P//oRcquwltB618hlz36p8B9FHEJWMR\nC9H73P4brW48TtSdZ8z0Jhb83gFTk/1wKq/hAP7q99ZWAohtytD8ejLFVycsGBd/\nHDY4GwThr0cEwzMpuLj7nG7xMuwflbrca+IVjTJ/Jg8OSXLiKJpiKGEHi/kv+KkU\nFBU48Xn+K6F5rEhBuau5\n=mJRq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-12T19:58:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followin